msgid ""
"# SLSTR VIS/SWIR Bands (S1–S6)\n"
"\n"
"Sentinel-3 SLSTR (Sea and Land Surface Temperature Radiometer) captures "
"Top-of-Atmosphere radiances in six solar reflective channels at 500 m "
"resolution: S1 (0.555 µm, vegetation/aerosol), S2 (0.659 µm, NDVI/aerosol), "
"S3 (0.865 µm, NDVI/cloud flagging), S4 (1.375 µm, cirrus detection), S5 "
"(1.61 µm, ice/snow/vegetation), and S6 (2.25 µm, vegetation state). Each "
"band is available in nadir and oblique views, enabling dual-angle "
"observation of land and ocean surfaces. The L1B product contains "
"geolocated, calibrated radiances produced by signal calibration, "
"re-gridding, and cloud flagging.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://sentiwiki.copernicus.eu/web/slstr-products#SLSTRProducts-L1"
"BProductsS3-SLSTR-Products-L1B)."
msgstr ""
"# SLSTR VIS/SWIR-bånd (S1–S6)\n"
"\n"
"Sentinel-3 SLSTR (Sea and Land Surface Temperature Radiometer) opfanger "
"radiansen i toppen af atmosfæren i seks solreflekterende kanaler ved 500 m "
"opløsning: S1 (0,555 µm, vegetation/aerosol), S2 (0,659 µm, NDVI/aerosol), "
"S3 (0,865 µm, NDVI/skymarkering), S4 (1,375 µm, cirrusdetektion), S5 (1,61 "
"µm, is/sne/vegetation) og S6 (2,25 µm, vegetationstilstand). Hvert bånd er "
"tilgængeligt i nadir- og skrå visning, hvilket muliggør observation af "
"land- og havoverflader i to vinkler. L1B-produktet indeholder "
"geolokaliseret, kalibreret radians frembragt ved signalkalibrering, "
"omgitring og skymarkering.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Mere info "
"[her](https://sentiwiki.copernicus.eu/web/slstr-products#SLSTRProducts-L1"
"BProductsS3-SLSTR-Products-L1B)."

msgid ""
"# SLSTR Thermal Infrared Bands (S7–S9)\n"
"\n"
"Sentinel-3 SLSTR (Sea and Land Surface Temperature Radiometer) captures "
"Top-of-Atmosphere brightness temperatures in three thermal infrared "
"channels at 1 km resolution: S7 (3.74 µm, sea/land surface temperature and "
"fire detection), S8 (10.85 µm, sea/land surface temperature and fire "
"detection), and S9 (12.0 µm, sea/land surface temperature). Each band is "
"available in nadir and oblique views, enabling dual-angle observation for "
"improved atmospheric correction and surface temperature retrieval. The L1B "
"product contains geolocated, calibrated brightness temperatures produced by "
"signal calibration, re-gridding, and cloud flagging.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://sentiwiki.copernicus.eu/web/slstr-products#SLSTRProducts-L1"
"BProductsS3-SLSTR-Products-L1B)."
msgstr ""
"# SLSTR termiske infrarøde bånd (S7–S9)\n"
"\n"
"Sentinel-3 SLSTR (Sea and Land Surface Temperature Radiometer) opfanger "
"lysstyrketemperaturer i toppen af atmosfæren i tre termiske infrarøde "
"kanaler ved 1 km opløsning: S7 (3,74 µm, hav-/landoverfladetemperatur og "
"branddetektion), S8 (10,85 µm, hav-/landoverfladetemperatur og "
"branddetektion) og S9 (12,0 µm, hav-/landoverfladetemperatur). Hvert bånd "
"er tilgængeligt i nadir- og skrå visning, hvilket muliggør observation i to "
"vinkler for forbedret atmosfærekorrektion og udledning af "
"overfladetemperatur. L1B-produktet indeholder geolokaliserede, kalibrerede "
"lysstyrketemperaturer frembragt ved signalkalibrering, omgitring og "
"skymarkering.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Mere info "
"[her](https://sentiwiki.copernicus.eu/web/slstr-products#SLSTRProducts-L1"
"BProductsS3-SLSTR-Products-L1B)."

msgid ""
"# Thermal IR fire emission bands\n"
"\n"
"Sentinel-3 Sea and Land Surface Temperature Instrument (SLSTR) has two "
"dedicated channels (F1 and F2) that aim to detect Land Surface Temperature "
"(LST). F2 Channel, with a central wavelength of 10854 nm measures in the "
"thermal infrared, or TIR. It is very useful for fire and high temperature "
"event monitoring at 1 km resolution.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://sentinel.esa.int/web/sentinel/user-guides/sentinel-3-slstr/"
"overview/geophysical-measurements/land-surface-temperature)"
msgstr ""
"# Termiske IR-brandemissionsbånd\n"
"\n"
"Sentinel-3 Sea and Land Surface Temperature Instrument (SLSTR) har to "
"dedikerede kanaler (F1 og F2), der har til formål at registrere "
"landoverfladetemperatur (LST). Kanal F2 med en central bølgelængde på 10854 "
"nm måler i det termiske infrarøde, eller TIR. Den er meget nyttig til "
"overvågning af brande og højtemperaturhændelser ved 1 km opløsning.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Mere info "
"[her.](https://sentinel.esa.int/web/sentinel/user-guides/sentinel-3-slstr/"
"overview/geophysical-measurements/land-surface-temperature)"

msgid ""
"# Cloud base height\n"
"\n"
"Height of cloud base measured in meters (m)."
msgstr ""
"# Skybasehøjde\n"
"\n"
"Højden af skybasen målt i meter (m)."

msgid ""
"# Cloud base pressure\n"
"\n"
"Pressure measured at cloud base in Pascal (Pa)."
msgstr ""
"# Skybasetryk\n"
"\n"
"Tryk målt ved skybasen i pascal (Pa)."

msgid ""
"# Effective radiometric cloud fraction\n"
"\n"
"Effective radiometric cloud fraction represents the portion of the Earth's "
"surface covered by clouds, divided by the total surface. Clouds have "
"shielding, albedo, and in-cloud absorption effects on trace gas retrieval. "
"The effective radiometric cloud fraction is an important parameter to "
"correct these effects."
msgstr ""
"# Effektiv radiometrisk skydækningsgrad\n"
"\n"
"Den effektive radiometriske skydækningsgrad angiver den del af Jordens "
"overflade, der er dækket af skyer, divideret med den samlede overflade. "
"Skyer har afskærmnings-, albedo- og absorptionseffekter i skyen på "
"bestemmelsen af sporgasser. Den effektive radiometriske skydækningsgrad er "
"en vigtig parameter til at korrigere for disse effekter."

msgid ""
"# Cloud optical thickness\n"
"\n"
"The cloud thickness is a key parameter to characterise optical properties "
"of clouds. It is a measure of how much sunlight passes through the cloud to "
"reach Earth's surface. The higher a cloud's optical thickness, the more "
"sunlight the cloud is scattering and reflecting. Dark blue shows where "
"there are low cloud optical thickness values and red shows larger cloud "
"optical thickness."
msgstr ""
"# Skyens optiske tykkelse\n"
"\n"
"Skytykkelsen er en nøgleparameter til at karakterisere skyers optiske "
"egenskaber. Den er et mål for, hvor meget sollys der passerer gennem skyen "
"og når Jordens overflade. Jo højere en skys optiske tykkelse er, desto mere "
"sollys spreder og reflekterer skyen. Mørkeblå viser, hvor der er lave "
"værdier for skyens optiske tykkelse, og rød viser større optisk tykkelse."

msgid ""
"# Cloud top height\n"
"\n"
"Height of cloud top measured in meters (m)."
msgstr ""
"# Skytophøjde\n"
"\n"
"Højden af skytoppen målt i meter (m)."

msgid ""
"# Cloud top pressure\n"
"\n"
"Pressure measured at cloud top in Pascal (Pa)."
msgstr ""
"# Skytoptryk\n"
"\n"
"Tryk målt ved skytoppen i pascal (Pa)."

msgid ""
"# Thermal band 10\n"
"\n"
"This thermal visualization is based on band 10 (a band is a region of the "
"electromagnetic spectrum; a satellite sensor can image Earth in different "
"bands). At the central wavelength of 10895 nm it measures in the thermal "
"infrared, or TIR. Instead of measuring the temperature of the air, like "
"weather stations do, band 10 reports on the ground itself, which is often "
"much hotter. Thermal band 10 is useful in providing surface temperatures "
"and is collected with a 100-meter resolution.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://www.usgs.gov/faqs/what-are-band-designations-landsat-"
"satellites?qt-news_science_products=0#qt-news_science_products)."
msgstr ""
"# Termisk bånd 10\n"
"\n"
"Denne termiske visualisering er baseret på bånd 10 (et bånd er et område af "
"det elektromagnetiske spektrum; en satellitsensor kan afbilde Jorden i "
"forskellige bånd). Ved den centrale bølgelængde på 10895 nm måler det i det "
"termiske infrarøde, eller TIR. I stedet for at måle luftens temperatur, som "
"vejrstationer gør, rapporterer bånd 10 om selve jorden, som ofte er meget "
"varmere. Termisk bånd 10 er nyttigt til at give overfladetemperaturer og "
"indsamles med en opløsning på 100 meter.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Mere info "
"[her](https://www.usgs.gov/faqs/what-are-band-designations-landsat-"
"satellites?qt-news_science_products=0#qt-news_science_products)."

msgid ""
"# Normalized Difference Vegetation Index (NDVI)\n"
"\n"
"The normalized difference vegetation index is a simple, but effective index "
"for quantifying green vegetation. It is a measure of the state of "
"vegetation health based on how plants reflect light at certain wavelengths. "
"The value range of the NDVI is -1 to 1. Negative values of NDVI (values "
"approaching -1) correspond to water. Values close to zero (-0.1to 0.1) "
"generally correspond to barren areas of rock, sand, or snow. Low, positive "
"values represent shrub and grassland (approximately 0.2 to 0.4), while high "
"values indicate temperate and tropical rainforests (values approaching 1).\n"
"\n"
"More info [here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/ndvi/)."
msgstr ""
"# Normalized Difference Vegetation Index (NDVI)\n"
"\n"
"Det normaliserede differensvegetationsindeks er et enkelt, men effektivt "
"indeks til kvantificering af grøn vegetation. Det er et mål for "
"vegetationens sundhedstilstand baseret på, hvordan planter reflekterer lys "
"ved bestemte bølgelængder. NDVI's værdiinterval er -1 til 1. Negative "
"NDVI-værdier (værdier nær -1) svarer til vand. Værdier tæt på nul (-0,1 til "
"0,1) svarer generelt til golde områder med klippe, sand eller sne. Lave, "
"positive værdier repræsenterer krat og græsland (ca. 0,2 til 0,4), mens "
"høje værdier indikerer tempererede og tropiske regnskove (værdier nær 1).\n"
"\n"
"Mere info [her](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/ndvi/)."

msgid ""
"# Enhanced Vegetation Index (EVI)\n"
"\n"
"The enhanced vegetation index (EVI) is an 'optimized' vegetation index as "
"it corrects for soil background signals and atmospheric influences. It is "
"very useful in areas of dense canopy cover. The range of values for EVI is "
"-1 to 1, with healthy vegetation generally around 0.20 to 0.80.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More infos [here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/evi/) "
"and [here.](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Enhanced_vegetation_index)"
msgstr ""
"# Enhanced Vegetation Index (EVI)\n"
"\n"
"Det forbedrede vegetationsindeks (EVI) er et 'optimeret' vegetationsindeks, "
"da det korrigerer for jordbundssignaler og atmosfæriske påvirkninger. Det "
"er meget nyttigt i områder med tæt kronedække. Værdiintervallet for EVI er "
"-1 til 1, hvor sund vegetation generelt ligger omkring 0,20 til 0,80.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Mere info [her](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/evi/) og "
"[her.](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Enhanced_vegetation_index)"

msgid ""
"# Atmospherically Resistant Vegetation Index (ARVI)\n"
"\n"
"The Atmospherically Resistant Vegetation Index (ARVI) is a vegetation index "
"that minimizes the effects of atmospheric scattering. It is most useful for "
"regions with high content of atmospheric aerosol (fog, dust, smoke, air "
"pollution). The range for an ARVI is -1 to 1 where green vegetation "
"generally falls between values of 0.20 to 0.80.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info [here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/arvi/) "
"and "
"[here.](https://eos.com/blog/6-spectral-indexes-on-top-of-ndvi-to-make-your-"
"vegetation-analysis-complete/)"
msgstr ""
"# Atmospherically Resistant Vegetation Index (ARVI)\n"
"\n"
"Det atmosfærisk modstandsdygtige vegetationsindeks (ARVI) er et "
"vegetationsindeks, der minimerer virkningerne af atmosfærisk spredning. Det "
"er mest nyttigt i regioner med højt indhold af atmosfærisk aerosol (tåge, "
"støv, røg, luftforurening). Intervallet for ARVI er -1 til 1, hvor grøn "
"vegetation generelt ligger mellem værdierne 0,20 og 0,80.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Mere info [her](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/arvi/) "
"og "
"[her.](https://eos.com/blog/6-spectral-indexes-on-top-of-ndvi-to-make-your-"
"vegetation-analysis-complete/)"

msgid ""
"# Soil Adjusted Vegetation Index (SAVI)\n"
"\n"
"The Soil Adjusted Vegetation Index is similar to Normalized Difference "
"Vegetation Index (NDVI) but is used in areas where vegetative cover is low "
"(< 40%). The index is a transformation technique that minimizes soil "
"brightness influences from spectral vegetation indices involving red and "
"near-infrared (NIR) wavelengths. The index is helpful when analysing young "
"crops, arid regions with sparse vegetation and exposed soil surfaces.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info [here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/savi/) "
"and "
"[here.](https://eos.com/blog/6-spectral-indexes-on-top-of-ndvi-to-make-your-"
"vegetation-analysis-complete/)"
msgstr ""
"# Soil Adjusted Vegetation Index (SAVI)\n"
"\n"
"Det jordjusterede vegetationsindeks ligner Normalized Difference Vegetation "
"Index (NDVI), men bruges i områder med lavt vegetationsdække (< 40 %). "
"Indekset er en transformationsteknik, der minimerer indflydelsen fra "
"jordens lysstyrke i spektrale vegetationsindeks, der involverer røde og "
"nær-infrarøde (NIR) bølgelængder. Indekset er nyttigt ved analyse af unge "
"afgrøder, tørre egne med spredt vegetation og blottede jordoverflader.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Mere info [her](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/savi/) "
"og "
"[her.](https://eos.com/blog/6-spectral-indexes-on-top-of-ndvi-to-make-your-"
"vegetation-analysis-complete/)"

msgid ""
"# Modified Anthocyanin Reflectance Index (mARI/ARI2)\n"
"\n"
"Anthocyanins are pigments common in higher plants, causing their red, blue "
"and purple coloration. They provide valuable information about the "
"physiological status of plants, as they are considered indicators of "
"various types of plant stresses. The reflectance of anthocyanin is highest "
"around 550nm. However, the same wavelengths are reflected by chlorophyll as "
"well. To isolate the anthocyanins, the 700nm spectral band, that reflects "
"only chlorophyll and not anthocyanins, is subtracted.\n"
"\n"
"To correct for leaf density and thickness, the near infrared spectral band "
"(in the recommended wavelengths of 760-800nm), which is related to leaf "
"scattering, is added to the basic ARI index. The new index is called "
"modified ARI or mARI (also ARI2).\n"
"\n"
"mARI values for the examined trees in [this original "
"article](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/mari/) ranged "
"in values from 0 to 8.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://digitalcommons.unl.edu/cgi/viewcontent.cgi?article=1227&"
"context=natrespapers)"
msgstr ""
"# Modified Anthocyanin Reflectance Index (mARI/ARI2)\n"
"\n"
"Anthocyaniner er pigmenter, der er almindelige i højere planter, og som "
"giver dem deres røde, blå og lilla farve. De giver værdifuld information om "
"planters fysiologiske tilstand, da de betragtes som indikatorer for "
"forskellige typer plantestress. Anthocyaniners reflektans er højest omkring "
"550 nm. Samme bølgelængder reflekteres dog også af klorofyl. For at isolere "
"anthocyaninerne trækkes 700 nm-spektralbåndet, der kun reflekterer klorofyl "
"og ikke anthocyaniner, fra.\n"
"\n"
"For at korrigere for bladtæthed og -tykkelse lægges det nær-infrarøde "
"spektralbånd (ved de anbefalede bølgelængder på 760-800 nm), som er "
"relateret til bladspredning, til det grundlæggende ARI-indeks. Det nye "
"indeks kaldes modificeret ARI eller mARI (også ARI2).\n"
"\n"
"mARI-værdierne for de undersøgte træer i [denne originale "
"artikel](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/mari/) lå i "
"intervallet 0 til 8.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Mere info "
"[her.](https://digitalcommons.unl.edu/cgi/viewcontent.cgi?article=1227&"
"context=natrespapers)"

msgid ""
"# Green City Script\n"
"\n"
"The Green city script aims to raise awareness of green areas in cities "
"around the world. The script takes into account the Normalized Difference "
"Vegetation Index (NDVI) and true color wavelengths; it separates built up "
"areas from vegetated ones, making it useful for detecting urban areas. "
"Built up areas are displayed in grey and vegetation is displayed in green.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/green_city/)"
msgstr ""
"# Green City Script\n"
"\n"
"Green city-scriptet har til formål at øge bevidstheden om grønne områder i "
"byer rundt om i verden. Scriptet tager højde for Normalized Difference "
"Vegetation Index (NDVI) og bølgelængder for naturtro farver; det adskiller "
"bebyggede områder fra beplantede og er derfor nyttigt til at registrere "
"byområder. Bebyggede områder vises i gråt, og vegetation vises i grønt.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Mere info "
"[her.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/green_city/)"

msgid ""
"# Urban Classified Script\n"
"\n"
"The Urban Classified script aims to detect built up areas by separating "
"them from barren ground, vegetation and water. Areas with a high moisture "
"content are returned in blue; areas indicating built up areas are returned "
"in white; vegetated areas are returned in green; everything else indicates "
"barren ground and is displayed in brown colors.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/urban_classified/"
")"
msgstr ""
"# Urban Classified Script\n"
"\n"
"Urban Classified-scriptet har til formål at registrere bebyggede områder "
"ved at adskille dem fra bar jord, vegetation og vand. Områder med højt "
"fugtindhold returneres i blåt; områder, der angiver bebyggelse, returneres "
"i hvidt; beplantede områder returneres i grønt; alt andet angiver bar jord "
"og vises i brune farver.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Mere info "
"[her.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/urban_classified/)"

msgid ""
"# Urban Land Infrared Color Script\n"
"\n"
"This script, made by Leo Tolari, combines true color visualization with "
"near infrared (NIR) and shortwave infrared (SWIR) wavelengths. The script "
"highlights urban areas better than true color, while still looking natural.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/urban_land_"
"infrared/)"
msgstr ""
"# Urban Land Infrared Color Script\n"
"\n"
"Dette script, lavet af Leo Tolari, kombinerer visualisering i naturtro "
"farver med nær-infrarøde (NIR) og kortbølgede infrarøde (SWIR) "
"bølgelængder. Scriptet fremhæver byområder bedre end naturtro farver, mens "
"det stadig ser naturligt ud.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Mere info "
"[her.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/urban_land_"
"infrared/)"

msgid ""
"# NDMI for Moisture Stress\n"
"\n"
"The Normalized Difference Moisture Index (NDMI) for moisture stress can be "
"used to detect irrigation. For all the index values above 0, knowing the "
"land use and land cover, it is possible to determine whether irrigation has "
"taken place. Knowing the type of crop grown (e.g. citrus crops), it is "
"possible to identify whether irrigation is being effective or not during "
"the crucial growing summer season, as well as find out if some parts of the "
"farm are being under or over-irrigated.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/ndmi_special/#)"
msgstr ""
"# NDMI for Moisture Stress\n"
"\n"
"Normalized Difference Moisture Index (NDMI) for fugtstress kan bruges til "
"at registrere kunstvanding. For alle indeksværdier over 0 er det, når man "
"kender arealanvendelsen og arealdækket, muligt at afgøre, om der har fundet "
"kunstvanding sted. Når man kender den dyrkede afgrødetype (f.eks. "
"citrusafgrøder), er det muligt at identificere, om kunstvandingen er "
"effektiv i den afgørende vækstsæson om sommeren, samt at finde ud af, om "
"dele af gården er under- eller overvandet.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Mere info "
"[her.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/ndmi_special/#)"

msgid ""
"# Normalized Difference Moisture Index (NDMI)\n"
"\n"
"The normalized difference moisture Index (NDMI) is used to determine "
"vegetation water content and monitor droughts. The value range of the NDMI "
"is -1 to 1. Negative values of NDMI (values approaching -1) correspond to "
"barren soil. Values around zero (-0.2 to 0.4) generally correspond to water "
"stress. High, positive values represent high canopy without water stress "
"(approximately 0.4 to 1).\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info [here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/ndmi/)"
msgstr ""
"# Normalized Difference Moisture Index (NDMI)\n"
"\n"
"Det normaliserede differensfugtindeks (NDMI) bruges til at bestemme "
"vegetationens vandindhold og overvåge tørke. NDMI's værdiinterval er -1 til "
"1. Negative NDMI-værdier (værdier nær -1) svarer til bar jord. Værdier "
"omkring nul (-0,2 til 0,4) svarer generelt til vandstress. Høje, positive "
"værdier repræsenterer tæt kronedække uden vandstress (ca. 0,4 til 1).\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Mere info [her.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/ndmi/)"

msgid ""
"# Normalized Difference Water Index (NDWI)\n"
"\n"
"The normalized difference water index is most appropriate for water body "
"mapping. Values of water bodies are larger than 0.5. Vegetation has smaller "
"values. Built-up features have positive values between zero and 0.2.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info [here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/ndwi/)"
msgstr ""
"# Normalized Difference Water Index (NDWI)\n"
"\n"
"Det normaliserede differensvandindeks er mest velegnet til kortlægning af "
"vandområder. Værdier for vandområder er større end 0,5. Vegetation har "
"mindre værdier. Bebyggede elementer har positive værdier mellem nul og 0,2.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Mere info [her.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/ndwi/)"

msgid ""
"# False color composite\n"
"\n"
"A false color composite uses at least one non-visible wavelength to image "
"Earth. The false color composite using near infrared, red and green bands "
"is very popular (a band is a region of the electromagnetic spectrum; a "
"satellite sensor can image Earth in different bands). The false colour "
"composite is most commonly used to assess plant density and health, since "
"plants reflect near infrared and green light, while they absorb red. Cities "
"and exposed ground are grey or tan, and water appears blue or black.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/false_color_"
"infrared/) and [here.](https://eo.belspo.be/en/colour-composites)"
msgstr ""
"# Falsk farvekomposit\n"
"\n"
"En falsk farvekomposit bruger mindst én usynlig bølgelængde til at afbilde "
"Jorden. Den falske farvekomposit med nær-infrarøde, røde og grønne bånd er "
"meget populær (et bånd er et område af det elektromagnetiske spektrum; en "
"satellitsensor kan afbilde Jorden i forskellige bånd). Den falske "
"farvekomposit bruges oftest til at vurdere plantetæthed og -sundhed, da "
"planter reflekterer nær-infrarødt og grønt lys, mens de absorberer rødt. "
"Byer og blottet jord er grå eller lysebrune, og vand fremstår blåt eller "
"sort.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Mere info "
"[her](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/false_color_"
"infrared/) og [her.](https://eo.belspo.be/en/colour-composites)"

msgid ""
"# False color composite\n"
"\n"
"A false color composite uses at least one non-visible wavelength to image "
"Earth. The false color composite using near infrared, red and green bands "
"is very popular (a band is a region of the electromagnetic spectrum; a "
"satellite sensor can image Earth in different bands). The false colour "
"composite is most commonly used to assess plant density and health, since "
"plants reflect near infrared and green light, while they absorb red. Cities "
"and exposed ground are grey or tan, and water appears blue or black.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/false_color_"
"infrared/)."
msgstr ""
"# Falsk farvekomposit\n"
"\n"
"En falsk farvekomposit bruger mindst én usynlig bølgelængde til at afbilde "
"Jorden. Den falske farvekomposit med nær-infrarøde, røde og grønne bånd er "
"meget populær (et bånd er et område af det elektromagnetiske spektrum; en "
"satellitsensor kan afbilde Jorden i forskellige bånd). Den falske "
"farvekomposit bruges oftest til at vurdere plantetæthed og -sundhed, da "
"planter reflekterer nær-infrarødt og grønt lys, mens de absorberer rødt. "
"Byer og blottet jord er grå eller lysebrune, og vand fremstår blåt eller "
"sort.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Mere info "
"[her](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/false_color_"
"infrared/)."

msgid ""
"# True color optimized\n"
"\n"
"This optimized True color script uses the visible light bands red, green "
"and blue in the corresponding red, green and blue color channels, resulting "
"in a product with natural colours that represents the Earth as humans would "
"naturally see it. The visualisation uses highlight compression and improves "
"the contrast and color vividness through minor contrast and saturation "
"enhancement.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info for "
"[L1C](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/l1c_optimized/) "
"and for "
"[L2A](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/l2a_optimized/)."
msgstr ""
"# Optimerede naturtro farver\n"
"\n"
"Dette optimerede script for naturtro farver bruger de synlige lysbånd rød, "
"grøn og blå i de tilsvarende røde, grønne og blå farvekanaler, hvilket "
"giver et produkt med naturlige farver, der gengiver Jorden, som mennesker "
"naturligt ville se den. Visualiseringen bruger komprimering af højlys og "
"forbedrer kontrasten og farvelivligheden gennem en mindre forøgelse af "
"kontrast og mætning.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Mere info for "
"[L1C](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/l1c_optimized/) og "
"for "
"[L2A](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/l2a_optimized/)."

msgid ""
"# True color composite\n"
"\n"
"Sensors carried by satellites can image Earth in different regions of the "
"electromagnetic spectrum. Each region in the spectrum is referred to as a "
"band. Landsat 8-9 has 11 bands. True color composite uses visible light "
"bands red, green and blue in the corresponding red, green and blue color "
"channels, resulting in a natural colored product, that is a good "
"representation of the Earth as humans would see it naturally.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/landsat-8/composites/)."
msgstr ""
"# Naturtro farvekomposit\n"
"\n"
"Sensorer båret af satellitter kan afbilde Jorden i forskellige områder af "
"det elektromagnetiske spektrum. Hvert område i spektret kaldes et bånd. "
"Landsat 8-9 har 11 bånd. Naturtro farvekomposit bruger de synlige lysbånd "
"rød, grøn og blå i de tilsvarende røde, grønne og blå farvekanaler, hvilket "
"giver et naturligt farvet produkt, der er en god gengivelse af Jorden, som "
"mennesker naturligt ville se den.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Mere info "
"[her](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/landsat-8/composites/)."

msgid ""
"# True color composite\n"
"\n"
"Sensors carried by satellites can image Earth in different regions of the "
"electromagnetic spectrum . Each region in the spectrum is referred to as a "
"band. True color composite uses visible light bands red, green and blue in "
"the corresponding red, green and blue color channels, resulting in a "
"natural colored product, that is a good representation of the Earth as "
"humans would see it naturally.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://sentinel.esa.int/web/sentinel/user-guides/sentinel-3-olci/"
"overview/heritage)"
msgstr ""
"# Naturtro farvekomposit\n"
"\n"
"Sensorer båret af satellitter kan afbilde Jorden i forskellige områder af "
"det elektromagnetiske spektrum. Hvert område i spektret kaldes et bånd. "
"Naturtro farvekomposit bruger de synlige lysbånd rød, grøn og blå i de "
"tilsvarende røde, grønne og blå farvekanaler, hvilket giver et naturligt "
"farvet produkt, der er en god gengivelse af Jorden, som mennesker naturligt "
"ville se den.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Mere info "
"[her.](https://sentinel.esa.int/web/sentinel/user-guides/sentinel-3-olci/"
"overview/heritage)"

msgid ""
"# Tristimulus\n"
"\n"
"The colours of natural waters differ markedly across the globe, depending "
"on water composition and illumination conditions. Ocean colour instruments "
"measure water-leaving radiance in narrow spectral bands to retrieve "
"water-quality indicators. The true colour of natural waters is derived by "
"calculating tristimulus values — the three primaries (X, Y, Z) that specify "
"a colour stimulus as perceived by the human eye.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-3/tristimulus/)."
msgstr ""
"# Tristimulus\n"
"\n"
"Farverne på naturligt vand varierer markant rundt om på kloden, afhængigt "
"af vandets sammensætning og belysningsforholdene. Instrumenter til havfarve "
"måler det udgående vandlys i smalle spektralbånd for at udlede "
"vandkvalitetsindikatorer. Naturligt vands sande farve udledes ved at "
"beregne tristimulusværdier — de tre primærfarver (X, Y, Z), der "
"specificerer en farvestimulus, som den opfattes af det menneskelige øje.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Mere info "
"[her](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-3/tristimulus/)."

msgid ""
"# RGB (B17, B05, B02)\n"
"\n"
"This false color composite maps Sentinel-3 OLCI bands B17 (865 nm, "
"near-infrared), B05 (510 nm, cyan-green), and B02 (412.5 nm, violet) into "
"the red, green, and blue display channels respectively. B17 is a "
"near-infrared band used for aerosol and atmospheric correction; placing it "
"in the red channel makes vegetation and land surfaces appear bright red "
"while water remains dark. B05 is sensitive to chlorophyll, sediment, "
"turbidity, and red tide, and B02 captures yellow dissolved organic matter "
"(CDOM) and detrital pigments. The composite is useful for ocean colour "
"analysis, coastal water quality monitoring, and distinguishing turbid or "
"sediment-laden waters from clear ocean.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info [here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-3/bands/)."
msgstr ""
"# RGB (B17, B05, B02)\n"
"\n"
"Denne falske farvekomposit kortlægger Sentinel-3 OLCI-båndene B17 (865 nm, "
"nær-infrarød), B05 (510 nm, cyangrøn) og B02 (412,5 nm, violet) til "
"henholdsvis den røde, grønne og blå visningskanal. B17 er et nær-infrarødt "
"bånd, der bruges til aerosol- og atmosfærekorrektion; når det placeres i "
"den røde kanal, fremstår vegetation og landoverflader klart røde, mens vand "
"forbliver mørkt. B05 er følsomt over for klorofyl, sediment, uklarhed og "
"rødt tidevand, og B02 opfanger gult opløst organisk stof (CDOM) og "
"detritale pigmenter. Kompositten er nyttig til analyse af havfarve, "
"overvågning af vandkvalitet i kystvande og til at skelne uklart eller "
"sedimentrigt vand fra klart hav.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Mere info [her](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-3/bands/)."

msgid ""
"# RGB (B17, B06, B03)\n"
"\n"
"This false color composite maps Sentinel-3 OLCI bands B17 (865 nm, "
"near-infrared), B06 (560 nm, green), and B03 (442.5 nm, blue) into the red, "
"green, and blue display channels respectively. B17 is a near-infrared band "
"used for aerosol and atmospheric correction; placing it in the red channel "
"makes vegetation and land surfaces appear bright red while water remains "
"dark. B06 is the chlorophyll absorption minimum reference band, and B03 "
"captures chlorophyll absorption and biogeochemical properties. Compared to "
"the B17/B05/B02 composite, the shifted green and blue channels offer a "
"different sensitivity to phytoplankton and dissolved organic matter in "
"coastal and open ocean waters.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info [here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-3/bands/)."
msgstr ""
"# RGB (B17, B06, B03)\n"
"\n"
"Denne falske farvekomposit kortlægger Sentinel-3 OLCI-båndene B17 (865 nm, "
"nær-infrarød), B06 (560 nm, grøn) og B03 (442,5 nm, blå) til henholdsvis "
"den røde, grønne og blå visningskanal. B17 er et nær-infrarødt bånd, der "
"bruges til aerosol- og atmosfærekorrektion; når det placeres i den røde "
"kanal, fremstår vegetation og landoverflader klart røde, mens vand "
"forbliver mørkt. B06 er referencebåndet for klorofylabsorptionens minimum, "
"og B03 opfanger klorofylabsorption og biogeokemiske egenskaber. "
"Sammenlignet med B17/B05/B02-kompositten giver de forskudte grønne og blå "
"kanaler en anden følsomhed over for fytoplankton og opløst organisk stof i "
"kystvande og åbent hav.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Mere info [her](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-3/bands/)."

msgid ""
"# Enhanced True Color Visualization\n"
"\n"
"This script uses highlight optimization to avoid burnt out pixels and to "
"even out the exposure. It makes clouds look natural and keep as much visual "
"information as possible. Sentinel-3 OLCI tiles cover large areas, making it "
"possible to observe large cloud formations, such as hurricanes.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-3/true_color_"
"highlight_optimized/)"
msgstr ""
"# Forbedret visualisering i naturtro farver\n"
"\n"
"Dette script bruger optimering af højlys for at undgå udbrændte pixels og "
"udjævne eksponeringen. Det får skyer til at se naturlige ud og bevarer så "
"megen visuel information som muligt. Sentinel-3 OLCI-felter dækker store "
"områder, hvilket gør det muligt at observere store skyformationer, såsom "
"orkaner.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Mere info "
"[her.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-3/true_color_"
"highlight_optimized/)"

msgid ""
"# Pansharpened True Color\n"
"\n"
"The pansharpened true color composite is done by using the usual true color "
"data (red, green and blue (RGB)) and enhancing them by using the "
"panchromatic band 8, or pan band (a band is a region of the electromagnetic "
"spectrum; a satellite sensor can image Earth in different bands). An image "
"from the pan band is similar to black-and-white film: it combines light "
"from the red, green, and blue parts of the spectrum into a single measure "
"of overall visible reflectance. Pansharpened images have 4x the resolution "
"of the usual true color composite, greatly enhancing the usefulness of "
"Landsat imagery.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://blog.mapbox.com/pansharpening-for-higher-resolution-in-"
"landsat-live-e4717cd7c356)."
msgstr ""
"# Pansharpened naturtro farver\n"
"\n"
"Den pansharpened naturtro farvekomposit fremstilles ved at bruge de "
"sædvanlige data i naturtro farver (rød, grøn og blå (RGB)) og forbedre dem "
"ved hjælp af det pankromatiske bånd 8, eller pan-båndet (et bånd er et "
"område af det elektromagnetiske spektrum; en satellitsensor kan afbilde "
"Jorden i forskellige bånd). Et billede fra pan-båndet ligner sort-hvid "
"film: det kombinerer lys fra de røde, grønne og blå dele af spektret til ét "
"enkelt mål for den samlede synlige reflektans. Pansharpened billeder har 4 "
"gange opløsningen af den sædvanlige naturtro farvekomposit, hvilket i høj "
"grad øger anvendeligheden af Landsat-billeder.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Mere info "
"[her](https://blog.mapbox.com/pansharpening-for-higher-resolution-in-"
"landsat-live-e4717cd7c356)."

msgid ""
"# False Color Urban composite\n"
"\n"
"This composite is used to visualise urbanized areas more clearly. "
"Vegetation is visible in shades of green, while urbanized areas are "
"represented by white, grey, or purple. Soils, sand, and minerals are shown "
"in a variety of colors. Snow and ice appear as dark blue, and water as "
"black or blue. Flooded areas are very dark blue and almost black. The "
"composite is useful for detecting wildfires and calderas of volcanoes, as "
"they are displayed in shades of red and yellow.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/false-color-urban-"
"rgb/) and [here.](https://eos.com/false-color/)"
msgstr ""
"# Falsk farvekomposit for byområder\n"
"\n"
"Denne komposit bruges til at visualisere urbaniserede områder tydeligere. "
"Vegetation er synlig i nuancer af grønt, mens urbaniserede områder "
"repræsenteres af hvidt, gråt eller lilla. Jord, sand og mineraler vises i "
"en række farver. Sne og is fremstår mørkeblå og vand sort eller blåt. "
"Oversvømmede områder er meget mørkeblå og næsten sorte. Kompositten er "
"nyttig til at registrere skovbrande og vulkankalderaer, da de vises i "
"nuancer af rødt og gult.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Mere info "
"[her](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/false-color-urban-"
"rgb/) og [her.](https://eos.com/false-color/)"

msgid ""
"# Agriculture composite\n"
"\n"
"This composite uses short-wave infrared, near-infrared and blue bands to "
"monitor crop health (a band is a region of the electromagnetic spectrum; a "
"satellite sensor can image Earth in different bands). Both short-wave and "
"near infrared bands are particularly good at highlighting dense vegetation, "
"which appears dark green in the composite. Crops appear in a vibrant green "
"and bare earth appears magenta.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info [here](https://eo.belspo.be/en/colour-composites) and "
"[here.](https://gisgeography.com/sentinel-2-bands-combinations/)"
msgstr ""
"# Landbrugskomposit\n"
"\n"
"Denne komposit bruger kortbølgede infrarøde, nær-infrarøde og blå bånd til "
"at overvåge afgrødesundhed (et bånd er et område af det elektromagnetiske "
"spektrum; en satellitsensor kan afbilde Jorden i forskellige bånd). Både "
"kortbølgede og nær-infrarøde bånd er særligt gode til at fremhæve tæt "
"vegetation, som fremstår mørkegrøn i kompositten. Afgrøder fremstår i en "
"levende grøn farve, og bar jord fremstår magenta.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Mere info [her](https://eo.belspo.be/en/colour-composites) og "
"[her.](https://gisgeography.com/sentinel-2-bands-combinations/)"

msgid ""
"# Snow Classifier\n"
"\n"
"The Snow Classifier algorithm aims to detect snow by classifying pixels "
"based on different brightness and Normalized Difference Snow Index (NDSI) "
"thresholds. Values classified as snow are returned in bright vivid blue. "
"The script can overestimate snow areas over clouds.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/snow_classifier/)"
msgstr ""
"# Snow Classifier\n"
"\n"
"Snow Classifier-algoritmen har til formål at registrere sne ved at "
"klassificere pixels ud fra forskellige tærskler for lysstyrke og Normalized "
"Difference Snow Index (NDSI). Værdier, der klassificeres som sne, "
"returneres i klar, levende blå. Scriptet kan overvurdere snearealer over "
"skyer.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Mere info "
"[her.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/snow_classifier/)"

msgid ""
"# Ulyssys Water Quality Viewer (UWQV)\n"
"\n"
"The script aims to dynamically visualise the chlorophyll and sediment "
"conditions of water bodies, which are primary indicators of water quality. "
"The chlorophyll content ranges in colors from dark blue (low chlorophyll "
"content) through green to red (high chlorophyll content). Sediment "
"concentrations are colored brown; opaque brown indicates high sediment "
"content.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/ulyssys_water_"
"quality_viewer/)"
msgstr ""
"# Ulyssys Water Quality Viewer (UWQV)\n"
"\n"
"Scriptet har til formål dynamisk at visualisere klorofyl- og "
"sedimentforholdene i vandområder, som er primære indikatorer for "
"vandkvalitet. Klorofylindholdet vises i farver fra mørkeblå (lavt "
"klorofylindhold) over grøn til rød (højt klorofylindhold). "
"Sedimentkoncentrationer farves brune; uigennemsigtig brun angiver højt "
"sedimentindhold.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Mere info "
"[her.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/ulyssys_water_"
"quality_viewer/)"

msgid ""
"# Short wave infrared composite (SWIR)\n"
"\n"
"Short wave infrared (SWIR) measurements can help scientists estimate how "
"much water is present in plants and soil, as water absorbs SWIR "
"wavelengths. Short wave infrared bands (a band is a region of the "
"electromagnetic spectrum; a satellite sensor can image Earth in different "
"bands) are also useful for distinguishing between cloud types (water clouds "
"versus ice clouds), snow and ice, all of which appear white in visible "
"light. In this composite vegetation appears in shades of green, soils and "
"built-up areas are in various shades of brown, and water appears black. "
"Newly burned land reflects strongly in SWIR bands, making them valuable for "
"mapping fire damages. Each rock type reflects shortwave infrared light "
"differently, making it possible to map out geology by comparing reflected "
"SWIR light.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/swir-rgb/)"
msgstr ""
"# Kortbølget infrarød komposit (SWIR)\n"
"\n"
"Målinger i kortbølget infrarød (SWIR) kan hjælpe forskere med at vurdere, "
"hvor meget vand der er i planter og jord, da vand absorberer "
"SWIR-bølgelængder. Kortbølgede infrarøde bånd (et bånd er et område af det "
"elektromagnetiske spektrum; en satellitsensor kan afbilde Jorden i "
"forskellige bånd) er også nyttige til at skelne mellem skytyper (vandskyer "
"i forhold til isskyer), sne og is, som alle fremstår hvide i synligt lys. I "
"denne komposit fremstår vegetation i nuancer af grønt, jord og bebyggede "
"områder i forskellige nuancer af brunt, og vand fremstår sort. Nyligt "
"afbrændt land reflekterer kraftigt i SWIR-bånd, hvilket gør dem værdifulde "
"til kortlægning af brandskader. Hver bjergart reflekterer kortbølget "
"infrarødt lys forskelligt, hvilket gør det muligt at kortlægge geologi ved "
"at sammenligne reflekteret SWIR-lys.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Mere info "
"[her.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/swir-rgb/)"

msgid ""
"# Normalised Difference Snow Index (NDSI)\n"
"\n"
"The Sentinel-2 normalised difference snow index can be used to "
"differentiate between cloud and snow cover as snow absorbs in the "
"short-wave infrared light, but reflects the visible light, whereas cloud is "
"generally reflective in both wavelengths. Snow cover is represented in "
"bright vivid blue.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info [here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/ndsi/)."
msgstr ""
"# Normalised Difference Snow Index (NDSI)\n"
"\n"
"Sentinel-2's normaliserede differenssneindeks kan bruges til at skelne "
"mellem sky- og snedække, da sne absorberer i det kortbølgede infrarøde lys, "
"men reflekterer det synlige lys, mens skyer generelt er reflekterende i "
"begge bølgelængder. Snedække repræsenteres i klar, levende blå.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Mere info [her](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/ndsi/)."

msgid ""
"# Normalised Difference Snow Index (NDSI)\n"
"\n"
"The normalised difference snow index (NDSI) can be used to differentiate "
"between cloud and snow cover as snow absorbs in the short-wave infrared "
"light, but reflects the visible light, whereas cloud is generally "
"reflective in both wavelengths. Snow cover is represented in bright vivid "
"blue.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info [here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/ndsi/)."
msgstr ""
"# Normalised Difference Snow Index (NDSI)\n"
"\n"
"Det normaliserede differenssneindeks (NDSI) kan bruges til at skelne mellem "
"sky- og snedække, da sne absorberer i det kortbølgede infrarøde lys, men "
"reflekterer det synlige lys, mens skyer generelt er reflekterende i begge "
"bølgelængder. Snedække repræsenteres i klar, levende blå.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Mere info [her](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/ndsi/)."

msgid ""
"# Highlight Optimized Natural Color\n"
"\n"
"This script aims to display the Earth in beautiful natural color images. It "
"uses highlight optimization to avoid burnt out pixels and to even out the "
"exposure.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://sentinel-hub.github.io/custom-scripts/sentinel-2/highlight_"
"optimized_natural_color/#)"
msgstr ""
"# Highlight Optimized Natural Color\n"
"\n"
"Dette script har til formål at vise Jorden i smukke billeder i naturlige "
"farver. Det bruger optimering af højlys for at undgå udbrændte pixels og "
"udjævne eksponeringen.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Mere info "
"[her.](https://sentinel-hub.github.io/custom-scripts/sentinel-2/highlight_"
"optimized_natural_color/#)"

msgid ""
"# Geology 12, 8, 2 composite\n"
"\n"
"This composite uses short-wave infrared (SWIR) band 12 to differentiate "
"among different rock types (a band is a region of the electromagnetic "
"spectrum; a satellite sensor can image Earth in different bands). Each rock "
"and mineral type reflects short-wave infrared light differently, making it "
"possible to map out geology by comparing reflected SWIR light. Near "
"infrared (NIR) band 8 highlights vegetation and band 2 detects moisture, "
"both contributing to differentiation of ground materials. The composite is "
"useful for finding geological formations and features (e.g. faults, "
"fractures), lithology (e.g. granite, basalt, etc.) and mining applications.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://www.euspaceimaging.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/06/EUSI-SWIR."
"pdf)"
msgstr ""
"# Geologi 12, 8, 2-komposit\n"
"\n"
"Denne komposit bruger kortbølget infrarødt (SWIR) bånd 12 til at skelne "
"mellem forskellige bjergarter (et bånd er et område af det "
"elektromagnetiske spektrum; en satellitsensor kan afbilde Jorden i "
"forskellige bånd). Hver bjergarts- og mineraltype reflekterer kortbølget "
"infrarødt lys forskelligt, hvilket gør det muligt at kortlægge geologi ved "
"at sammenligne reflekteret SWIR-lys. Nær-infrarødt (NIR) bånd 8 fremhæver "
"vegetation, og bånd 2 registrerer fugt, hvilket begge bidrager til at "
"skelne jordmaterialer. Kompositten er nyttig til at finde geologiske "
"formationer og træk (f.eks. forkastninger, brud), litologi (f.eks. granit, "
"basalt osv.) og til minedrift.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Mere info "
"[her.](https://www.euspaceimaging.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/06/EUSI-SWIR."
"pdf)"

msgid ""
"# Geology 8, 11, 12 composite\n"
"\n"
"This composite uses both short-wave infrared (SWIR) bands 11 and 12 to "
"differentiate among different rock types (a band is a region of the "
"electromagnetic spectrum; a satellite sensor can image Earth in different "
"bands). Each rock and mineral type reflects shortwave infrared light "
"differently, making it possible to map out geology by comparing reflected "
"SWIR light. Near Infrared (NIR) band 8 highlights vegetation, contributing "
"to differentiation of ground materials. Vegetation in the composite appears "
"red. The composite is useful for differentiating vegetation, and land "
"especially geologic features that can be useful for mining and mineral "
"exploration.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info [here.](http://murphygeological.com/new---sentinel-2.html#)"
msgstr ""
"# Geologi 8, 11, 12-komposit\n"
"\n"
"Denne komposit bruger både kortbølgede infrarøde (SWIR) bånd 11 og 12 til "
"at skelne mellem forskellige bjergarter (et bånd er et område af det "
"elektromagnetiske spektrum; en satellitsensor kan afbilde Jorden i "
"forskellige bånd). Hver bjergarts- og mineraltype reflekterer kortbølget "
"infrarødt lys forskelligt, hvilket gør det muligt at kortlægge geologi ved "
"at sammenligne reflekteret SWIR-lys. Nær-infrarødt (NIR) bånd 8 fremhæver "
"vegetation, hvilket bidrager til at skelne jordmaterialer. Vegetation "
"fremstår rød i kompositten. Kompositten er nyttig til at skelne vegetation "
"og land, især geologiske træk, der kan være nyttige til minedrift og "
"efterforskning af mineraler.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Mere info [her.](http://murphygeological.com/new---sentinel-2.html#)"

msgid ""
"# Wildfires\n"
"\n"
"This script, created by Pierre Markuse, visualizes wildfires using "
"Sentinel-2 data. It combines natural color background with some NIR/SWIR "
"data for smoke penetration and more detail, while adding highlights from "
"B11 and B12 to show fires in red and orange colors.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/custom-scripts/sentinel-2/"
"markuse_fire/)"
msgstr ""
"# Skovbrande\n"
"\n"
"Dette script, skabt af Pierre Markuse, visualiserer skovbrande ved hjælp af "
"Sentinel-2-data. Det kombinerer en baggrund i naturlige farver med nogle "
"NIR/SWIR-data for at trænge gennem røg og give flere detaljer, mens det "
"tilføjer højlys fra B11 og B12 for at vise brande i røde og orange farver.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Mere info "
"[her.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/custom-scripts/sentinel-2/"
"markuse_fire/)"

msgid ""
"# Wildfires\n"
"\n"
"This script, based on the Pierre Markuse wildfire script, detects and "
"visualizes wildfires using Landsat 8/9 thermal and visible bands. It "
"combines natural color (B2, B3, B4) with thermal band (B10) analysis to "
"detect temperature anomalies and create a red-orange-white glow effect "
"highlighting fire locations.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://github.com/azlinszkysinergise/customscripts_test_az/blob/"
"main/landsat_markuse_fire_v2)"
msgstr ""
"# Skovbrande\n"
"\n"
"Dette script, baseret på Pierre Markuses skovbrandsscript, registrerer og "
"visualiserer skovbrande ved hjælp af termiske og synlige Landsat 8/9-bånd. "
"Det kombinerer naturlige farver (B2, B3, B4) med analyse af termisk bånd "
"(B10) for at registrere temperaturanomalier og skabe en rød-orange-hvid "
"glødeeffekt, der fremhæver brandenes placering.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Mere info "
"[her.](https://github.com/azlinszkysinergise/customscripts_test_az/blob/"
"main/landsat_markuse_fire_v2)"

msgid ""
"# Enhanced True Color\n"
"\n"
"This script, created by Pierre Markuse, uses multiple bands (a band is a "
"region of the electromagnetic spectrum; a satellite sensor can image Earth "
"in different bands) and saturation and brightness control to enhance the "
"true color visualization.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-3/enhanced_true_"
"color-2/#)"
msgstr ""
"# Forbedrede naturtro farver\n"
"\n"
"Dette script, skabt af Pierre Markuse, bruger flere bånd (et bånd er et "
"område af det elektromagnetiske spektrum; en satellitsensor kan afbilde "
"Jorden i forskellige bånd) samt kontrol af mætning og lysstyrke til at "
"forbedre visualiseringen i naturtro farver.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Mere info "
"[her.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-3/enhanced_true_"
"color-2/#)"

msgid ""
"# Burned Area Index\n"
"\n"
"Burned Area Index takes advantage of the wider spectrum of Visible, "
"Red-Edge, NIR and SWIR bands.\n"
"\n"
"Values description:()=> The range of values for the index is `-1` to `1` "
"for burn scars, and `1` - `6` for active fires. Different fire intensities "
"may result in different thresholds; the current values were calibrated, as "
"per original author, on mostly Mediterranen regions.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info [here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/bais2/)"
msgstr ""
"# Burned Area Index\n"
"\n"
"Burned Area Index udnytter det bredere spektrum af synlige, red-edge-, NIR- "
"og SWIR-bånd.\n"
"\n"
"Værdibeskrivelse:()=> Indeksets værdiinterval er `-1` til `1` for brandar "
"og `1` - `6` for aktive brande. Forskellige brandintensiteter kan give "
"forskellige tærskler; de nuværende værdier blev ifølge den oprindelige "
"forfatter kalibreret hovedsageligt på middelhavsregioner.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Mere info [her.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/bais2/)"

msgid ""
"# Normalized Burn Ratio (NBR)\n"
"\n"
"Normalized Burn Ratio is frequently used to estimate burn severity. It uses "
"near-infrared (NIR) and shortwave-infrared (SWIR) wavelengths. Healthy "
"vegetation has a high reflectance in the near-infrared portion of the "
"spectrum, and a low short-wave infrared reflectance. On the other hand, "
"burned areas have a high shortwave infrared reflectance but low reflectance "
"in the near infrared Darker pixels indicate burned areas.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/custom-scripts/sentinel-2/"
"nbr/)."
msgstr ""
"# Normalized Burn Ratio (NBR)\n"
"\n"
"Normalized Burn Ratio bruges ofte til at vurdere brandens alvorlighed. Det "
"bruger nær-infrarøde (NIR) og kortbølgede infrarøde (SWIR) bølgelængder. "
"Sund vegetation har en høj reflektans i den nær-infrarøde del af spektret "
"og en lav reflektans i kortbølget infrarødt. Omvendt har afbrændte områder "
"en høj reflektans i kortbølget infrarødt, men lav reflektans i "
"nær-infrarødt. Mørkere pixels angiver afbrændte områder.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Mere info "
"[her](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/custom-scripts/sentinel-2/nbr/"
")."

msgid ""
"# Atmospheric penetration\n"
"\n"
"This composite uses different bands (a band is a region of the "
"electromagnetic spectrum; a satellite sensor can image Earth in different "
"bands) in the non-visible part of the electromagnetic spectrum to reduce "
"the influence of the atmosphere in the image. Short wave infrared bands 11 "
"and 12 are highly reflected by the heated areas, making them useful for "
"fire and burned area mapping. Near infrared band 8, is on contrary, highly "
"reflected by vegetation, which signifies absence of fire. Vegetation "
"appears blue, displaying details related to the vegetation vigor. Healthy "
"vegetation is shown in light blue while the stressed, sparse or/and arid "
"vegetation appears in dull blue. Urban features are white, grey, cyan or "
"purple.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info [here.](https://eos.com/atmospheric-penetration/)"
msgstr ""
"# Atmosfærisk penetration\n"
"\n"
"Denne komposit bruger forskellige bånd (et bånd er et område af det "
"elektromagnetiske spektrum; en satellitsensor kan afbilde Jorden i "
"forskellige bånd) i den ikke-synlige del af det elektromagnetiske spektrum "
"for at reducere atmosfærens indflydelse på billedet. Kortbølgede infrarøde "
"bånd 11 og 12 reflekteres kraftigt af opvarmede områder, hvilket gør dem "
"nyttige til kortlægning af brande og afbrændte områder. Nær-infrarødt bånd "
"8 reflekteres derimod kraftigt af vegetation, hvilket betyder fravær af "
"brand. Vegetation fremstår blå og viser detaljer relateret til "
"vegetationens vitalitet. Sund vegetation vises i lyseblå, mens stresset, "
"sparsom og/eller tør vegetation fremstår i mat blå. Byelementer er hvide, "
"grå, cyan eller lilla.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Mere info [her.](https://eos.com/atmospheric-penetration/)"

msgid ""
"# Barren Soil Visualization\n"
"\n"
"The Barren Soil Visualization can be useful for soil mapping, to "
"investigate the location of landslides or the extent of erosion in "
"non-vegetated areas. This visualization shows all vegetation in green and "
"the barren ground in red. Water appears black.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/barren_soil/) and "
"[here.](https://medium.com/sentinel-hub/create-useful-and-beautiful-"
"satellite-images-with-custom-scripts-8ef0e6a474c6)"
msgstr ""
"# Visualisering af bar jord\n"
"\n"
"Visualiseringen af bar jord kan være nyttig til jordkortlægning, til at "
"undersøge placeringen af jordskred eller omfanget af erosion i områder uden "
"vegetation. Denne visualisering viser al vegetation i grønt og den bare "
"jord i rødt. Vand fremstår sort.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Mere info "
"[her](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/barren_soil/) og "
"[her.](https://medium.com/sentinel-hub/create-useful-and-beautiful-"
"satellite-images-with-custom-scripts-8ef0e6a474c6)"

msgid ""
"# True Color with IR Highlights composite\n"
"\n"
"This composite enhances the true color visualization by adding the "
"shortwave infrared wavelengths to amplify details. It displays heated areas "
"in red/orange.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://medium.com/sentinel-hub/active-volcanoes-as-seen-from-space-"
"9d1de0133733)"
msgstr ""
"# Naturtro farver med IR-højlys-komposit\n"
"\n"
"Denne komposit forbedrer visualiseringen i naturtro farver ved at tilføje "
"de kortbølgede infrarøde bølgelængder for at forstærke detaljer. Den viser "
"opvarmede områder i rødt/orange.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Mere info "
"[her.](https://medium.com/sentinel-hub/active-volcanoes-as-seen-from-space-9"
"d1de0133733)"

msgid ""
"# Detection of Burned Areas\n"
"\n"
"This script is used to detect large scale recently burned areas. Pixels "
"colored red highlight burned areas, and all other pixels are returned in "
"true color. The script sometimes overestimates burned areas over water and "
"clouds.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/burned_area_ms/)"
msgstr ""
"# Registrering af afbrændte områder\n"
"\n"
"Dette script bruges til at registrere store, nyligt afbrændte områder. "
"Pixels farvet røde fremhæver afbrændte områder, og alle andre pixels "
"returneres i naturtro farver. Scriptet overvurderer nogle gange afbrændte "
"områder over vand og skyer.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Mere info "
"[her.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/burned_area_ms/)"

msgid ""
"# Scene classification\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Scene classification was developed to distinguish between cloudy pixels, "
"clear pixels and water pixels of Sentinel-2 data and is a result of ESA's "
"Scene classification algorithm. Twelve different classifications are "
"provided including classes of clouds, vegetation, soils/desert, water and "
"snow. It does not constitute a land cover classification map in a strict "
"sense.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/scene-"
"classification/)."
msgstr ""
"# Sceneklassificering\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Sceneklassificering blev udviklet til at skelne mellem skyede pixels, klare "
"pixels og vandpixels i Sentinel-2-data og er et resultat af ESA's "
"sceneklassificeringsalgoritme. Der leveres tolv forskellige "
"klassifikationer, herunder klasser for skyer, vegetation, jord/ørken, vand "
"og sne. Det udgør ikke et arealdækkekort i streng forstand.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Mere info "
"[her](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/scene-"
"classification/)."

msgid ""
"# Terrestrial Chlorophyll Index (OTCI)\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"The Terrestrial Chlorophyll Index (OTCI) is estimated based on the "
"chlorophyll content in terrestrial vegetation and can be used to monitor "
"vegetation condition and health. Low OTCI values usually signify water, "
"sand or snow. Extremely high values, displayed with white, usually suggest "
"the absence of chlorophyll as well. They generally represent either bare "
"ground, rock or clouds. The chlorophyll values in between range from red "
"(low chlorophyll values) to dark green (high chlorophyll values) can be "
"used to determine vegetation health.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info [here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-3/otci/)"
msgstr ""
"# Terrestrial Chlorophyll Index (OTCI)\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Det terrestriske klorofylindeks (OTCI) estimeres ud fra klorofylindholdet i "
"terrestrisk vegetation og kan bruges til at overvåge vegetationens tilstand "
"og sundhed. Lave OTCI-værdier angiver normalt vand, sand eller sne. "
"Ekstremt høje værdier, vist med hvid, tyder normalt også på fravær af "
"klorofyl. De repræsenterer generelt enten bar jord, klippe eller skyer. "
"Klorofylværdierne derimellem, fra rød (lave klorofylværdier) til mørkegrøn "
"(høje klorofylværdier), kan bruges til at bestemme vegetationens sundhed.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Mere info [her.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-3/otci/)"

msgid ""
"# Topographic Visualization\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"This script returns a visualisation with green colours representing lowland "
"elevations and earth colours as mountainous elevations. The script uses "
"discrete classes rather than the continuous visualisations in the other DEM "
"layers.\n"
"\n"
"It is possible to set custom min and max values in the evalscript by "
"setting defaultVis to false and setting the min and max variables to the "
"desired values.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/dem/dem-topographic/)"
msgstr ""
"# Topografisk visualisering\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Dette script returnerer en visualisering, hvor grønne farver repræsenterer "
"lavtliggende terræn og jordfarver repræsenterer bjergrige højder. Scriptet "
"bruger diskrete klasser i stedet for de kontinuerte visualiseringer i de "
"andre DEM-lag.\n"
"\n"
"Det er muligt at angive brugerdefinerede min- og maks-værdier i "
"evalscriptet ved at sætte defaultVis til false og sætte variablerne min og "
"max til de ønskede værdier.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Mere info "
"[her.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/dem/dem-topographic/)"

msgid ""
"# Color Visualization\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"This script returns a color visualization of a digital elevation model, "
"assigning continuous colors to the elevation borders.\n"
"\n"
"It is possible to set custom min and max values in the evalscript by "
"setting defaultVis to false and setting the min and max variables to the "
"desired values.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info [here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/dem/dem-color/)"
msgstr ""
"# Farvevisualisering\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Dette script returnerer en farvevisualisering af en digital højdemodel og "
"tildeler kontinuerte farver til højdegrænserne.\n"
"\n"
"Det er muligt at angive brugerdefinerede min- og maks-værdier i "
"evalscriptet ved at sætte defaultVis til false og sætte variablerne min og "
"max til de ønskede værdier.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Mere info [her.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/dem/dem-color/)"

