msgid ""
"# Enhanced visualization\n"
"\n"
"This script combines the gamma0 of the VV and VH polarizations into a false "
"color visualization. It displays water areas in blue (partially black) and "
"land in different shades of yellow/green. Urban areas are displayed in a "
"light green-yellow (towards white), vegetated areas in mustard green and "
"bare ground in a darker green.\n"
"\n"
"For snowy and icy areas, the visualization can vary from light green-yellow "
"over brighter green to dark brown or even black. In order not to confuse "
"cryogenic features with non-cryogenic ones, some general information about "
"the location is helpful in interpreting the image."
msgstr ""
"# Forbedret visualisering\n"
"\n"
"Dette script kombinerer gamma0 for VV- og VH-polariseringerne til en "
"visualisering i falske farver. Det viser vandområder i blåt (delvist sort) "
"og land i forskellige nuancer af gult/grønt. Byområder vises i en lys "
"grøngul farve (mod hvid), beplantede områder i sennepsgrønt og bar jord i "
"en mørkere grøn.\n"
"\n"
"For sne- og isdækkede områder kan visualiseringen variere fra lys grøngul "
"over lysere grøn til mørkebrun eller endda sort. For ikke at forveksle "
"kryogene træk med ikke-kryogene er nogle generelle oplysninger om stedet "
"nyttige ved fortolkning af billedet."

msgid ""
"# SAR False Color Visualization\n"
"\n"
"This script combines the gamma0 of the VV and VH polarizations of "
"Sentinel-1 SAR data into a false color visualization. Water areas appear in "
"blue (partially black) and land in different shades of yellow/green. Urban "
"areas are displayed in light green-yellow (towards white), vegetated areas "
"in mustard green, and bare ground in darker green. The visualization "
"supports a wide range of monitoring applications, including ice and ship "
"tracking, agriculture and deforestation monitoring, and emergency response "
"scenarios such as flood and volcano observation.\n"
"\n"
"For snowy and icy areas, the visualization can vary from light green-yellow "
"over brighter green to dark brown or even black. Some general knowledge of "
"the location is helpful to avoid confusing cryogenic features with other "
"land cover types.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-1/sar_false_color_"
"visualization/)."
msgstr ""
"# SAR-visualisering i falske farver\n"
"\n"
"Dette script kombinerer gamma0 for VV- og VH-polariseringerne i Sentinel-1 "
"SAR-data til en visualisering i falske farver. Vandområder fremstår i blåt "
"(delvist sort) og land i forskellige nuancer af gult/grønt. Byområder vises "
"i lys grøngul (mod hvid), beplantede områder i sennepsgrønt og bar jord i "
"mørkere grøn. Visualiseringen understøtter en bred vifte af "
"overvågningsanvendelser, herunder sporing af is og skibe, overvågning af "
"landbrug og skovrydning samt nødberedskabsscenarier som observation af "
"oversvømmelser og vulkaner.\n"
"\n"
"For sne- og isdækkede områder kan visualiseringen variere fra lys grøngul "
"over lysere grøn til mørkebrun eller endda sort. Kendskab til stedet er "
"nyttigt for at undgå at forveksle kryogene træk med andre arealdækketyper.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Mere info "
"[her](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-1/sar_false_color_"
"visualization/)."

msgid ""
"# Urban Areas\n"
"\n"
"This script uses Sentinel-1 SAR VH and VV polarisations to highlight urban "
"areas and buildings. Structures appear in different colours depending on "
"their backscatter characteristics: purple indicates high VH reflectance, "
"green indicates high VV reflectance, and white indicates high reflectance "
"in both. The red channel is restricted to pixels where VH exceeds 0.5, "
"helping separate buildings from bare soil. The script is useful for "
"monitoring urban expansion, assessing building density, and identifying "
"structures in flood-prone areas. Note that in mountainous terrain, steep "
"slopes and snow can produce similar signals, making it difficult to "
"separate urban areas from other features.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-1/urban_areas/)."
msgstr ""
"# Byområder\n"
"\n"
"Dette script bruger Sentinel-1 SAR VH- og VV-polariseringer til at fremhæve "
"byområder og bygninger. Strukturer fremstår i forskellige farver afhængigt "
"af deres backscatter-egenskaber: lilla angiver høj VH-reflektans, grøn "
"angiver høj VV-reflektans, og hvid angiver høj reflektans i begge. Den røde "
"kanal er begrænset til pixels, hvor VH overstiger 0,5, hvilket hjælper med "
"at adskille bygninger fra bar jord. Scriptet er nyttigt til overvågning af "
"byudvidelse, vurdering af bebyggelsestæthed og identifikation af strukturer "
"i oversvømmelsestruede områder. Bemærk, at i bjergrigt terræn kan stejle "
"skråninger og sne give lignende signaler, hvilket gør det vanskeligt at "
"adskille byområder fra andre træk.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Mere info "
"[her](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-1/urban_areas/)."

msgid ""
"# SAR Deforestation Detection\n"
"\n"
"This script processes Sentinel-1 VV and VH polarisation bands to detect "
"deforestation and forest degradation. It converts the backscatter values "
"into polar form to derive vector length and angle, which discriminate "
"between water, forest, and bare soil. Water and bare soil appear black, "
"forested areas are rendered in green gradients, and degraded or cleared "
"areas appear in red — with stronger colours indicating higher "
"classification confidence. The script is useful for monitoring forest loss "
"and land-use change over time.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-1/sar_deforestation_"
"detection/)."
msgstr ""
"# SAR-registrering af skovrydning\n"
"\n"
"Dette script behandler Sentinel-1 VV- og VH-polariseringsbånd for at "
"registrere skovrydning og skovforringelse. Det omregner "
"backscatter-værdierne til polær form for at udlede vektorlængde og vinkel, "
"som skelner mellem vand, skov og bar jord. Vand og bar jord fremstår sorte, "
"skovklædte områder gengives i grønne gradienter, og forringede eller "
"ryddede områder fremstår røde — med stærkere farver, der angiver højere "
"klassificeringssikkerhed. Scriptet er nyttigt til overvågning af skovtab og "
"ændringer i arealanvendelse over tid.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Mere info "
"[her](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-1/sar_deforestation_"
"detection/)."

msgid ""
"# Water Surface Roughness\n"
"\n"
"This script visualizes water surface roughness using Sentinel-1 SAR data. "
"SAR backscatter is highly sensitive to the roughness of the water surface: "
"calm water reflects radar energy away from the sensor and appears dark, "
"while rough or wind-driven water scatters energy back and appears brighter. "
"Variations in surface roughness reveal oceanographic and maritime features "
"such as wind patterns, sea currents, internal waves, and ship wakes. Oil "
"spills dampen surface waves and appear as dark patches against the "
"surrounding rougher water. The visualization supports maritime monitoring "
"applications including ship tracking, oil pollution detection, and "
"observation of ocean circulation.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-1/water_surface_"
"roughness_visualization/)."
msgstr ""
"# Vandoverfladens ruhed\n"
"\n"
"Dette script visualiserer vandoverfladens ruhed ved hjælp af Sentinel-1 "
"SAR-data. SAR-backscatter er meget følsom over for vandoverfladens ruhed: "
"roligt vand reflekterer radarenergi væk fra sensoren og fremstår mørkt, "
"mens oprørt eller vinddrevet vand spreder energi tilbage og fremstår "
"lysere. Variationer i overfladens ruhed afslører oceanografiske og maritime "
"træk såsom vindmønstre, havstrømme, interne bølger og skibsbølger. "
"Olieudslip dæmper overfladebølger og fremstår som mørke pletter mod det "
"omgivende ruere vand. Visualiseringen understøtter maritime "
"overvågningsanvendelser, herunder sporing af skibe, registrering af "
"olieforurening og observation af havcirkulation.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Mere info "
"[her](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-1/water_surface_"
"roughness_visualization/)."

msgid ""
"# RGB ratio\n"
"\n"
"This script combines the gamma0 of the VV and VH polarizations into a false "
"color visualization. It uses the VV polarization in the red channel, the VH "
"polarization in the green channel, and a ratio of VH/VV in the blue "
"channel. It shows water areas in dark red (black), urban areas in yellow, "
"vegetated areas in turquoise, and bare ground in dark purple.\n"
"\n"
"For snowy and icy areas, the visualization can vary from light yellow to "
"blue to red. In order not to confuse cryogenic features with non-cryogenic "
"ones, some general information about the location is helpful in "
"interpreting the image."
msgstr ""
"# RGB-forhold\n"
"\n"
"Dette script kombinerer gamma0 for VV- og VH-polariseringerne til en "
"visualisering i falske farver. Det bruger VV-polariseringen i den røde "
"kanal, VH-polariseringen i den grønne kanal og et forhold mellem VH/VV i "
"den blå kanal. Det viser vandområder i mørkerød (sort), byområder i gult, "
"beplantede områder i turkis og bar jord i mørk lilla.\n"
"\n"
"For sne- og isdækkede områder kan visualiseringen variere fra lysegul til "
"blå til rød. For ikke at forveksle kryogene træk med ikke-kryogene er nogle "
"generelle oplysninger om stedet nyttige ved fortolkning af billedet."

msgid ""
"# SAR Urban\n"
"\n"
"The script is useful for locating urban areas and individual buildings. It "
"uses the gamma0 of the VH polarization and the VV polarizations to "
"highlight different buildings and topology orientations with purple and "
"green colors. It can be used to track urban expansion, estimate building "
"type, or locate buildings in risk areas (e.g., flooding).\n"
"\n"
"For snowy and icy areas, the visualization can vary from white to purple to "
"dark blue or even black. In order not to confuse cryogenic features with "
"non-cryogenic ones, some general information about the location is helpful "
"to interpret the image. \n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-1/urban_areas/)."
msgstr ""
"# SAR byområder\n"
"\n"
"Scriptet er nyttigt til at lokalisere byområder og enkelte bygninger. Det "
"bruger gamma0 for VH-polariseringen og VV-polariseringerne til at fremhæve "
"forskellige bygninger og topologiorienteringer med lilla og grønne farver. "
"Det kan bruges til at følge byudvidelse, vurdere bygningstype eller "
"lokalisere bygninger i risikoområder (f.eks. oversvømmelse).\n"
"\n"
"For sne- og isdækkede områder kan visualiseringen variere fra hvid til "
"lilla til mørkeblå eller endda sort. For ikke at forveksle kryogene træk "
"med ikke-kryogene er nogle generelle oplysninger om stedet nyttige til at "
"fortolke billedet. \n"
"\n"
"Mere info "
"[her](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-1/urban_areas/)."

msgid ""
"# HH - decibel gamma0\n"
"\n"
"This script displays a grayscale visualization of the gamma0 of the HH "
"polarization. The HH polarization is less sensitive to surface roughness "
"compared to the VV polarization and is therefore used for detecting objects "
"and hard targets such as ships. It provides good contrast between water and "
"land surfaces. Compared to the linear gamma0 visualization, the decibel "
"gamma0 visualization includes a logarithmic scaling of the data."
msgstr ""
"# HH - decibel gamma0\n"
"\n"
"Dette script viser en gråtonevisualisering af gamma0 for HH-polariseringen. "
"HH-polariseringen er mindre følsom over for overfladens ruhed sammenlignet "
"med VV-polariseringen og bruges derfor til at registrere objekter og hårde "
"mål såsom skibe. Den giver god kontrast mellem vand- og landoverflader. "
"Sammenlignet med den lineære gamma0-visualisering omfatter "
"decibel-gamma0-visualiseringen en logaritmisk skalering af dataene."

msgid ""
"# HH - linear gamma0\n"
"\n"
"This script displays a grayscale visualization of the gamma0 of the HH "
"polarization. The HH polarization is less sensitive to surface roughness "
"compared to the VV polarization and is therefore used for detecting objects "
"and hard targets such as ships."
msgstr ""
"# HH - lineær gamma0\n"
"\n"
"Dette script viser en gråtonevisualisering af gamma0 for HH-polariseringen. "
"HH-polariseringen er mindre følsom over for overfladens ruhed sammenlignet "
"med VV-polariseringen og bruges derfor til at registrere objekter og hårde "
"mål såsom skibe."

msgid ""
"# HV - decibel gamma0\n"
"\n"
"This script displays a grayscale visualization of the gamma0 of the HV "
"polarization. The values for the cross polarization (HV) are generally "
"lower (darker visualization) than for the co-polarization (HH, VV). The HV "
"polarization has higher values for surfaces characterized by volume "
"scattering, e.g., branches, dry coil bodies, or canopies (lighter color in "
"the visualization) and lower for surfaces with little to no scattering "
"(darker color in the visualization). Compared to the linear gamma0 "
"visualization, the decibel gamma0 visualization includes a logarithmic "
"scaling of the data."
msgstr ""
"# HV - decibel gamma0\n"
"\n"
"Dette script viser en gråtonevisualisering af gamma0 for HV-polariseringen. "
"Værdierne for krydspolariseringen (HV) er generelt lavere (mørkere "
"visualisering) end for co-polariseringen (HH, VV). HV-polariseringen har "
"højere værdier for overflader, der er kendetegnet ved volumenspredning, "
"f.eks. grene, tørre jordlegemer eller kronedække (lysere farve i "
"visualiseringen), og lavere for overflader med lidt eller ingen spredning "
"(mørkere farve i visualiseringen). Sammenlignet med den lineære "
"gamma0-visualisering omfatter decibel-gamma0-visualiseringen en logaritmisk "
"skalering af dataene."

msgid ""
"# HV - linear gamma0\n"
"\n"
"This script displays a grayscale visualization of the gamma0 of the HV "
"polarization. The values for the cross polarization (HV) are generally "
"lower (darker visualization) than for the co-polarization (HH, VV). The HV "
"polarization has higher values for surfaces characterized by volume "
"scattering, e.g., branches, dry coil bodies, or canopies (lighter color in "
"the visualization) and lower for surfaces with little to no scattering "
"(darker color in the visualization)."
msgstr ""
"# HV - lineær gamma0\n"
"\n"
"Dette script viser en gråtonevisualisering af gamma0 for HV-polariseringen. "
"Værdierne for krydspolariseringen (HV) er generelt lavere (mørkere "
"visualisering) end for co-polariseringen (HH, VV). HV-polariseringen har "
"højere værdier for overflader, der er kendetegnet ved volumenspredning, "
"f.eks. grene, tørre jordlegemer eller kronedække (lysere farve i "
"visualiseringen), og lavere for overflader med lidt eller ingen spredning "
"(mørkere farve i visualiseringen)."

msgid ""
"# VH - decibel gamma0\n"
"\n"
"This script displays a grayscale visualization of the gamma0 of the VH "
"polarization. The values for the cross polarization (VH) are generally "
"lower (darker visualization) than for the co-polarization (HH, VV). The VH "
"polarization has higher values for surfaces characterized by volume "
"scattering, e.g., branches, dry coil bodies, or canopies (lighter color in "
"the visualization) and lower for surfaces with little to no scattering "
"(darker color in the visualization). Compared to the linear gamma0 "
"visualization, the decibel gamma0 visualization includes a logarithmic "
"scaling of the data."
msgstr ""
"# VH - decibel gamma0\n"
"\n"
"Dette script viser en gråtonevisualisering af gamma0 for VH-polariseringen. "
"Værdierne for krydspolariseringen (VH) er generelt lavere (mørkere "
"visualisering) end for co-polariseringen (HH, VV). VH-polariseringen har "
"højere værdier for overflader, der er kendetegnet ved volumenspredning, "
"f.eks. grene, tørre jordlegemer eller kronedække (lysere farve i "
"visualiseringen), og lavere for overflader med lidt eller ingen spredning "
"(mørkere farve i visualiseringen). Sammenlignet med den lineære "
"gamma0-visualisering omfatter decibel-gamma0-visualiseringen en logaritmisk "
"skalering af dataene."

msgid ""
"# VH - linear gamma0\n"
"\n"
"This script displays a grayscale visualization of the gamma0 of the VH "
"polarization. The values for the cross polarization (VH) are generally "
"lower (darker visualization) than for the co-polarization (HH, VV).  The VH "
"polarization has higher values for surfaces characterized by volume "
"scattering, e.g., branches, dry coil bodies, or canopies (lighter color in "
"the visualization) and lower for surfaces with little to no scattering "
"(darker color in the visualization)."
msgstr ""
"# VH - lineær gamma0\n"
"\n"
"Dette script viser en gråtonevisualisering af gamma0 for VH-polariseringen. "
"Værdierne for krydspolariseringen (VH) er generelt lavere (mørkere "
"visualisering) end for co-polariseringen (HH, VV).  VH-polariseringen har "
"højere værdier for overflader, der er kendetegnet ved volumenspredning, "
"f.eks. grene, tørre jordlegemer eller kronedække (lysere farve i "
"visualiseringen), og lavere for overflader med lidt eller ingen spredning "
"(mørkere farve i visualiseringen)."

msgid ""
"# VV - decibel gamma0\n"
"\n"
"This script displays a grayscale visualization of the gamma0 of the VV "
"polarization. Compared to the HH polarization, the VV polarization is more "
"sensitive to surface roughness and is therefore often used in the detection "
"of oil contamination or wake detection. Compared to the linear gamma0 "
"visualization, the decibel gamma0 visualization includes a logarithmic "
"scaling of the data."
msgstr ""
"# VV - decibel gamma0\n"
"\n"
"Dette script viser en gråtonevisualisering af gamma0 for VV-polariseringen. "
"Sammenlignet med HH-polariseringen er VV-polariseringen mere følsom over "
"for overfladens ruhed og bruges derfor ofte til registrering af "
"olieforurening eller skibsbølger. Sammenlignet med den lineære "
"gamma0-visualisering omfatter decibel-gamma0-visualiseringen en logaritmisk "
"skalering af dataene."

msgid ""
"# VV - linear gamma0\n"
"\n"
"This script displays a grayscale visualization of the gamma0 of the VV "
"polarization. Compared to the HH polarization, the VV polarization is more "
"sensitive to surface roughness and is therefore often used in the detection "
"of oil contamination or wake detection."
msgstr ""
"# VV - lineær gamma0\n"
"\n"
"Dette script viser en gråtonevisualisering af gamma0 for VV-polariseringen. "
"Sammenlignet med HH-polariseringen er VV-polariseringen mere følsom over "
"for overfladens ruhed og bruges derfor ofte til registrering af "
"olieforurening eller skibsbølger."

msgid ""
"# Total suspended matter concentration\n"
"\n"
"Satellite-derived total suspended matter (TSM) is a measure of the "
"concentration of particulate material in surface water such as mud, silt "
"and other fine-grainded sedimentss, including organic and inorganic "
"fractions. The TSM product is calculated based on the MERIS 1999 Baseline "
"Atmospheric Correction and the OCI neural net TSM algorithm by [Hieronymi "
"et al. "
"2017](https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/marine-science/articles/10.3389/"
"fmars.2017.00140/full). The product has variable accuracy and schould be "
"considert experimental.\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://documentation.dataspace.copernicus.eu/Data/SentinelMissions/"
"Sentinel3.html#sentinel-3-olci-level-2)"
msgstr ""
"# Koncentration af total suspenderet stof\n"
"\n"
"Satellitebaseret total suspenderet stof (TSM) er et mål for koncentrationen "
"af partikulært materiale i overfladevand, såsom mudder, silt og andre "
"finkornede sedimenter, herunder organiske og uorganiske fraktioner. "
"TSM-produktet beregnes på grundlag af MERIS 1999 Baseline Atmospheric "
"Correction og OCI-neuralnetværksalgoritmen for TSM af [Hieronymi et al. "
"2017](https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/marine-science/articles/10.3389/"
"fmars.2017.00140/full). Produktet har varierende nøjagtighed og bør "
"betragtes som eksperimentelt.\n"
"\n"
"Mere info "
"[her.](https://documentation.dataspace.copernicus.eu/Data/SentinelMissions/"
"Sentinel3.html#sentinel-3-olci-level-2)"

msgid ""
"# Aerosol optical thickness\n"
"\n"
"Aerosol optical thickness (AOT) is a measure of the extent to which "
"aerosols in the atmosphere prevent the transmission of light through "
"absorption and scattering. Optical thickness, also knwon as optical depth "
"depends on the physical nature, the shape and the concentration of "
"particles. AOT is often used in climatology and atmospheric research to "
"assess the effects of aerosols on weather, climate, and air quality.\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://user.eumetsat.int/resources/user-guides/sentinel-3-ocean-"
"colour-level-2-data-guide#ID-Data)"
msgstr ""
"# Aerosols optiske tykkelse\n"
"\n"
"Aerosols optiske tykkelse (AOT) er et mål for, i hvilket omfang aerosoler i "
"atmosfæren forhindrer lysets transmission gennem absorption og spredning. "
"Optisk tykkelse, også kendt som optisk dybde, afhænger af partiklernes "
"fysiske natur, form og koncentration. AOT bruges ofte i klimatologi og "
"atmosfæreforskning til at vurdere aerosolers indvirkning på vejr, klima og "
"luftkvalitet.\n"
"\n"
"Mere info "
"[her.](https://user.eumetsat.int/resources/user-guides/sentinel-3-ocean-"
"colour-level-2-data-guide#ID-Data)"

msgid ""
"# Photosynthetically active radiation\n"
"\n"
"The Photosynthetically Active Radiation (PAR) visualization displays the "
"instantaneous PAR at the water surface. It was adopted from FERIS and "
"developed based on an algorithm by [Aiken and Moore "
"(1997)](https://earth.esa.int/eogateway/documents/20142/37627/MERIS_ATBD_2.1"
"8_v4.0+-+1997+-+PAR.pdf/07a8cd54-94ba-4efe-fe9a-751d1ffc9381). The PAR is a "
"measure of the energy flux from the sun in the wavelenght range of 400–700 "
"nm. It is often used to convert measured chlorophyll concentration into an "
"estimate of ocen productivity and from this an estimate of the carbon "
"sequestration. As such, it plays an important role in modelling of the "
"carbon-cycle.\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://user.eumetsat.int/resources/user-guides/sentinel-3-ocean-"
"colour-level-2-data-guide#ID-Data)."
msgstr ""
"# Fotosyntetisk aktiv stråling\n"
"\n"
"Visualiseringen af fotosyntetisk aktiv stråling (PAR) viser den "
"øjeblikkelige PAR ved vandoverfladen. Den er overtaget fra FERIS og "
"udviklet på grundlag af en algoritme af [Aiken og Moore "
"(1997)](https://earth.esa.int/eogateway/documents/20142/37627/MERIS_ATBD_2.1"
"8_v4.0+-+1997+-+PAR.pdf/07a8cd54-94ba-4efe-fe9a-751d1ffc9381). PAR er et "
"mål for energifluxen fra solen i bølgelængdeområdet 400–700 nm. Den bruges "
"ofte til at omregne målt klorofylkoncentration til et estimat af havets "
"produktivitet og ud fra det et estimat af kulstofbindingen. Som sådan "
"spiller den en vigtig rolle i modellering af kulstofkredsløbet.\n"
"\n"
"Mere info "
"[her](https://user.eumetsat.int/resources/user-guides/sentinel-3-ocean-"
"colour-level-2-data-guide#ID-Data)."

msgid ""
"# Diffuse attenuation coefficient\n"
"\n"
"The diffuse attenuation coefficient at 490 nm is a measure of how the "
"intensity of light decreases as it passes through a column of water. It "
"quantifies the rate at which light is absorbed and scattered by water and "
"its constituents, such as phytoplankton, dissolved organic matter and "
"suspended particles. This coefficient is crucial for understanding "
"underwater light environments and is widely used in marine biology, "
"oceanography and environmental science. It's calculated as described in "
"[Morel et al. "
"(2007)](https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0034425707001"
"307).\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://user.eumetsat.int/resources/user-guides/sentinel-3-ocean-"
"colour-level-2-data-guide#ID-Data)."
msgstr ""
"# Diffus dæmpningskoefficient\n"
"\n"
"Den diffuse dæmpningskoefficient ved 490 nm er et mål for, hvordan lysets "
"intensitet aftager, når det passerer gennem en vandsøjle. Den kvantificerer "
"den hastighed, hvormed lys absorberes og spredes af vand og dets "
"bestanddele, såsom fytoplankton, opløst organisk stof og suspenderede "
"partikler. Denne koefficient er afgørende for forståelsen af lysforholdene "
"under vand og bruges bredt inden for marinbiologi, oceanografi og "
"miljøvidenskab. Den beregnes som beskrevet i [Morel et al. "
"(2007)](https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0034425707001"
"307).\n"
"\n"
"Mere info "
"[her](https://user.eumetsat.int/resources/user-guides/sentinel-3-ocean-"
"colour-level-2-data-guide#ID-Data)."

msgid ""
"# Integrated water vapour column\n"
"\n"
"The integrated water vapour column displays the water vapour integrated "
"over an atmosphere column. It is displayed in kg/m2 and calculated on the "
"basis of band 18 (885 nm) and band 19 (900 nm). The product shows an "
"overestimation in the transition zones between glint and off-glint and has "
"a systematic overestimation of about 20%.\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://sentiwiki.copernicus.eu/web/olci-products#OLCIProducts-"
"IntegratedWaterVapourColumnoverLandS3-OLCI-Products-L2-Land-IWV)."
msgstr ""
"# Integreret vanddampsøjle\n"
"\n"
"Den integrerede vanddampsøjle viser vanddampen integreret over en "
"atmosfæresøjle. Den vises i kg/m2 og beregnes på grundlag af bånd 18 (885 "
"nm) og bånd 19 (900 nm). Produktet viser en overvurdering i "
"overgangszonerne mellem glint og off-glint og har en systematisk "
"overvurdering på omkring 20 %.\n"
"\n"
"Mere info "
"[her](https://sentiwiki.copernicus.eu/web/olci-products#OLCIProducts-"
"IntegratedWaterVapourColumnoverLandS3-OLCI-Products-L2-Land-IWV)."

msgid ""
"# Algal pigment concentration (open waters)\n"
"\n"
"Ocean Colour for MERIS (OC4Me) developed by [Morel et al. "
"(2007)](https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0034425707001"
"307) and CI developed by [Hu et al. "
"(2012)](https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1029/2011JC007395).\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://user.eumetsat.int/resources/user-guides/sentinel-3-ocean-"
"colour-level-2-data-guide#ID-Data)."
msgstr ""
"# Koncentration af algepigment (åbent vand)\n"
"\n"
"Ocean Colour for MERIS (OC4Me) udviklet af [Morel et al. "
"(2007)](https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0034425707001"
"307) og CI udviklet af [Hu et al. "
"(2012)](https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1029/2011JC007395).\n"
"\n"
"Mere info "
"[her](https://user.eumetsat.int/resources/user-guides/sentinel-3-ocean-"
"colour-level-2-data-guide#ID-Data)."

msgid ""
"# Algal pigment concentration (complex waters)\n"
"\n"
"Ocean Colour for MERIS (OC4Me) developed by [Morel et al. "
"(2007)](https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0034425707001"
"307) and CI developed by [Hu et al. "
"(2012)](https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1029/2011JC007395).\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://user.eumetsat.int/resources/user-guides/sentinel-3-ocean-"
"colour-level-2-data-guide#ID-Data)."
msgstr ""
"# Koncentration af algepigment (komplekst vand)\n"
"\n"
"Ocean Colour for MERIS (OC4Me) udviklet af [Morel et al. "
"(2007)](https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0034425707001"
"307) og CI udviklet af [Hu et al. "
"(2012)](https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1029/2011JC007395).\n"
"\n"
"Mere info "
"[her](https://user.eumetsat.int/resources/user-guides/sentinel-3-ocean-"
"colour-level-2-data-guide#ID-Data)."

msgid ""
"# CDM absorption coefficient\n"
"\n"
"The Coloured Detrital and Dissolved Material (CDM) absorption coefficient "
"at 443 nm indicates the fraction of incident light that is absorbed by both "
"detrital particles and colored dissolved organic matter (CDOM). Dissolved "
"organic matter is an important component of the oceanic carbon cycle. It is "
"also used as an indicator for assessing the impact of terrigenous inputs in "
"coastal waters.\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://data.jrc.ec.europa.eu/dataset/b2c93f4d-7d90-448f-a6f4-62f78e3"
"b673b)."
msgstr ""
"# CDM-absorptionskoefficient\n"
"\n"
"Absorptionskoefficienten for Coloured Detrital and Dissolved Material (CDM) "
"ved 443 nm angiver den andel af det indfaldende lys, der absorberes af både "
"detritale partikler og farvet opløst organisk stof (CDOM). Opløst organisk "
"stof er en vigtig komponent i havets kulstofkredsløb. Det bruges også som "
"indikator til vurdering af virkningen af terrigene tilførsler i kystvande.\n"
"\n"
"Mere info "
"[her](https://data.jrc.ec.europa.eu/dataset/b2c93f4d-7d90-448f-a6f4-62f78e3"
"b673b)."

msgid ""
"# Aerosol Angstrom exponent\n"
"\n"
"The Aerosol Angstrom exponent is a parameter that describes how the optical "
"thickness of aerosols in the atmosphere varies with wavelength. It provides "
"information about the size distribution of aerosol particles, with higher "
"values indicating smaller particles and lower values indicating larger "
"particles. This exponent is often used in atmospheric research and "
"climatology to analyse the properties of aerosols and their effects on "
"climate and air quality.\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://user.eumetsat.int/resources/user-guides/sentinel-3-ocean-"
"colour-level-2-data-guide#ID-Data)"
msgstr ""
"# Aerosols Ångström-eksponent\n"
"\n"
"Aerosols Ångström-eksponent er en parameter, der beskriver, hvordan den "
"optiske tykkelse af aerosoler i atmosfæren varierer med bølgelængden. Den "
"giver oplysninger om størrelsesfordelingen af aerosolpartikler, hvor højere "
"værdier angiver mindre partikler og lavere værdier angiver større "
"partikler. Denne eksponent bruges ofte i atmosfæreforskning og klimatologi "
"til at analysere aerosolers egenskaber og deres indvirkning på klima og "
"luftkvalitet.\n"
"\n"
"Mere info "
"[her.](https://user.eumetsat.int/resources/user-guides/sentinel-3-ocean-"
"colour-level-2-data-guide#ID-Data)"

msgid ""
"# Rectified reflectance 779\n"
"\n"
"The rectified reflectance product is a by-product of the GIFAPAR product. "
"It shows a virtual reflectance that is largely free of atmospheric and "
"angular effects and is a good approcimation of the top of the canopy "
"reflectances. The rectified reflectance 779 is based on the NIR band (band "
"17) with a wavelength of 779 nm.\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://sentiwiki.copernicus.eu/web/olci-products#OLCIProducts-"
"RectifiedReflectanceS3-OLCI-Products-L2-Land-RC)."
msgstr ""
"# Korrigeret reflektans 779\n"
"\n"
"Produktet for korrigeret reflektans er et biprodukt af GIFAPAR-produktet. "
"Det viser en virtuel reflektans, der i vid udstrækning er fri for "
"atmosfæriske og vinkelmæssige effekter, og som er en god tilnærmelse til "
"reflektansen i toppen af kronedækket. Den korrigerede reflektans 779 er "
"baseret på NIR-båndet (bånd 17) med en bølgelængde på 779 nm.\n"
"\n"
"Mere info "
"[her](https://sentiwiki.copernicus.eu/web/olci-products#OLCIProducts-"
"RectifiedReflectanceS3-OLCI-Products-L2-Land-RC)."

msgid ""
"# Rectified reflectance 681\n"
"\n"
"The rectified reflectance product is a by-product of the GIFAPAR product. "
"It shows a virtual reflectance that is largely free of atmospheric and "
"angular effects and is a good approcimation of the top of the canopy "
"reflectances. The rectified reflectance 681 is based on the red band (band "
"10) with a wavelength of 681 nm.\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://sentiwiki.copernicus.eu/web/olci-products#OLCIProducts-"
"RectifiedReflectanceS3-OLCI-Products-L2-Land-RC)."
msgstr ""
"# Korrigeret reflektans 681\n"
"\n"
"Produktet for korrigeret reflektans er et biprodukt af GIFAPAR-produktet. "
"Det viser en virtuel reflektans, der i vid udstrækning er fri for "
"atmosfæriske og vinkelmæssige effekter, og som er en god tilnærmelse til "
"reflektansen i toppen af kronedækket. Den korrigerede reflektans 681 er "
"baseret på det røde bånd (bånd 10) med en bølgelængde på 681 nm.\n"
"\n"
"Mere info "
"[her](https://sentiwiki.copernicus.eu/web/olci-products#OLCIProducts-"
"RectifiedReflectanceS3-OLCI-Products-L2-Land-RC)."

msgid ""
"# Green Instantaneous Fraction of Absorbed Photosynthetically Available "
"Radiation (GIFAPAR)\n"
"\n"
"The Green Instantaneous Fraction of Absorbed Photosynthetically Available "
"Radiation (GIFAPAR) is a bio-geophysical product used to study the "
"photosynthetic process of plants and is often used in diagnostic and "
"predictive models computing primary productivity of the vegetation "
"canopies. In addition, this parameter is also an input for the estimation "
"of assimilation of CO2 in vegetation. GIFAPAR ranges from 0–1.\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://sentiwiki.copernicus.eu/web/olci-products#OLCIProducts-"
"GreenInstantaneousFractionofAbsorbedPhotosyntheticallyActiveRadiation(GI-"
"FAPAR)S3-OLCI-Products-L2-Land-GI-FAPAR)."
msgstr ""
"# Green Instantaneous Fraction of Absorbed Photosynthetically Available "
"Radiation (GIFAPAR)\n"
"\n"
"Green Instantaneous Fraction of Absorbed Photosynthetically Available "
"Radiation (GIFAPAR) er et biogeofysisk produkt, der bruges til at studere "
"planters fotosyntese, og som ofte anvendes i diagnostiske og prædiktive "
"modeller, der beregner den primære produktivitet i vegetationens "
"kronedække. Desuden er denne parameter et input til estimeringen af "
"CO2-assimilation i vegetation. GIFAPAR ligger mellem 0 og 1.\n"
"\n"
"Mere info "
"[her](https://sentiwiki.copernicus.eu/web/olci-products#OLCIProducts-"
"GreenInstantaneousFractionofAbsorbedPhotosyntheticallyActiveRadiation(GI-"
"FAPAR)S3-OLCI-Products-L2-Land-GI-FAPAR)."

msgid ""
"# Integrated water vapour column\n"
"\n"
"The integrated water vapour column displays the water vapour integrated "
"over an atmosphere column. It is displayed in kg/m2 and calculated on the "
"basis of band 18 (885 nm) and band 19 (900 nm). The product provides stable "
"and high quality results, but shows a systematic overestimation of about "
"9%–13% copared to ground base reference.\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://sentiwiki.copernicus.eu/web/olci-products#OLCIProducts-"
"IntegratedWaterVapourColumnoverLandS3-OLCI-Products-L2-Land-IWV)."
msgstr ""
"# Integreret vanddampsøjle\n"
"\n"
"Den integrerede vanddampsøjle viser vanddampen integreret over en "
"atmosfæresøjle. Den vises i kg/m2 og beregnes på grundlag af bånd 18 (885 "
"nm) og bånd 19 (900 nm). Produktet giver stabile resultater af høj "
"kvalitet, men viser en systematisk overvurdering på omkring 9 %–13 % "
"sammenlignet med jordbaseret reference.\n"
"\n"
"Mere info "
"[her](https://sentiwiki.copernicus.eu/web/olci-products#OLCIProducts-"
"IntegratedWaterVapourColumnoverLandS3-OLCI-Products-L2-Land-IWV)."

msgid ""
"# Land Surface Temperature (LST)\n"
"\n"
"The Land Surface Temperature (LST) product provides the temperature of the "
"Earth's surface as retrieved from the SLSTR thermal infrared channels. LST "
"is a key parameter in the physics of land surface, controlling the "
"partitioning of energy between the atmosphere and the land surface. It is "
"used in climate change monitoring, drought monitoring, and urban heat "
"island studies.\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://sentiwiki.copernicus.eu/web/slstr-products#S3-SLSTR-Products-"
"L2-LST-Products)."
msgstr ""
"# Landoverfladetemperatur (LST)\n"
"\n"
"Produktet for landoverfladetemperatur (LST) angiver temperaturen på Jordens "
"overflade, udledt af SLSTR's termiske infrarøde kanaler. LST er en "
"nøgleparameter i landoverfladens fysik og styrer fordelingen af energi "
"mellem atmosfæren og landoverfladen. Den bruges til overvågning af "
"klimaændringer, tørkeovervågning og undersøgelser af bymæssige varmeøer.\n"
"\n"
"Mere info "
"[her](https://sentiwiki.copernicus.eu/web/slstr-products#S3-SLSTR-Products-"
"L2-LST-Products)."

msgid ""
"# Normalized Difference Vegetation Index (NDVI)\n"
"\n"
"The Normalized Difference Vegetation Index (NDVI) is a dimensionless index "
"that describes the difference between visible and near-infrared reflectance "
"of vegetation cover. It can be used to estimate the density of vegetation "
"cover and monitor vegetation health.\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://github.com/eu-cdse/sentinel-hub-custom-scripts/tree/main/"
"sentinel-3/slstrl2/ndvi/)."
msgstr ""
"# Normalized Difference Vegetation Index (NDVI)\n"
"\n"
"Normalized Difference Vegetation Index (NDVI) er et dimensionsløst indeks, "
"der beskriver forskellen mellem vegetationsdækkets synlige og nær-infrarøde "
"reflektans. Det kan bruges til at estimere vegetationsdækkets tæthed og "
"overvåge vegetationens sundhed.\n"
"\n"
"Mere info "
"[her](https://github.com/eu-cdse/sentinel-hub-custom-scripts/tree/main/"
"sentinel-3/slstrl2/ndvi/)."

msgid ""
"The Normalized Difference Vegetation Index is a spectral index indicating "
"the greenness of the vegetation."
msgstr ""
"Normalized Difference Vegetation Index er et spektralt indeks, der angiver "
"vegetationens grønhed."

msgid ""
"Number of clear-sky surface reflectance used for the inversion of the "
"bidirectional reflectance distribution function."
msgstr ""
"Antal reflektansværdier for overfladen under klar himmel, der er brugt til "
"inversionen af den bidirektionelle reflektansfordelingsfunktion."

msgid ""
"Uncertainty of the NDVI is calculated by propagating the uncertainties "
"associated to the model parameters resulting from the inversion of the "
"bidirectional reflectance distribution function."
msgstr ""
"Usikkerheden på NDVI beregnes ved at propagere de usikkerheder, der er "
"knyttet til modelparametrene, som følger af inversionen af den "
"bidirektionelle reflektansfordelingsfunktion."

msgid "The Burn Scar layer indicates detected burn scars for a given day."
msgstr "Laget Burn Scar angiver registrerede brandar for en given dag."

msgid "The Burn Scar layer indicates detected burn scars for a given month."
msgstr "Laget Burn Scar angiver registrerede brandar for en given måned."

msgid "Fraction of pixel surface affected by fire at the day of the burn detection."
msgstr ""
"Andel af pixelfladen, der er berørt af brand på dagen for "
"brandregistreringen."

msgid ""
"Fraction of pixel surface affected by fire at the month of the burn "
"detection."
msgstr ""
"Andel af pixelfladen, der er berørt af brand i måneden for "
"brandregistreringen."

msgid "Probability that the burn detection corresponds to an actual burn."
msgstr "Sandsynlighed for, at brandregistreringen svarer til en faktisk brand."

msgid "Day of burn in year (1-366), no burn (0) or flag (<0)."
msgstr "Dag for brand i året (1-366), ingen brand (0) eller flag (<0)."

msgid "Probability that the fractional burned area is above 0.1."
msgstr "Sandsynlighed for, at den afbrændte andel af arealet er over 0,1."

msgid "Probability that the fractional burned area is above 0.1˝."
msgstr "Sandsynlighed for, at den afbrændte andel af arealet er over 0,1˝."

msgid ""
"DMP, or Dry Matter Productivity, represents the overall growth rate or dry "
"biomass increase of the vegetation, expressed in kilograms of dry matter "
"per hectare per day (kgDM/ha/day). DMP is directly related to NPP (Net "
"Primary Productivity, in gC/m²/day), but its units are customized for "
"agro-statistical purposes. "
msgstr ""
"DMP, eller Dry Matter Productivity (tørstofproduktivitet), repræsenterer "
"vegetationens samlede vækstrate eller stigning i tør biomasse, udtrykt i "
"kilogram tørstof pr. hektar pr. dag (kgDM/ha/dag). DMP er direkte relateret "
"til NPP (Net Primary Productivity, i gC/m²/dag), men dens enheder er "
"tilpasset agro-statistiske formål. "

msgid ""
"FAPAR corresponds to the fraction of photosynthetically active radiation "
"absorbed by the green elements of the canopy. The FAPAR value results "
"directly from the radiative transfer model in the canopy which is computed "
"instantaneously. It depends on canopy structure, vegetation element optical "
"properties and illumination conditions. FAPAR is very useful as input to a "
"number of primary productivity models based on simple efficiency "
"considerations."
msgstr ""
"FAPAR svarer til den andel af den fotosyntetisk aktive stråling, der "
"absorberes af kronedækkets grønne elementer. FAPAR-værdien følger direkte "
"af strålingstransportmodellen i kronedækket, som beregnes øjeblikkeligt. "
"Den afhænger af kronedækkets struktur, vegetationselementernes optiske "
"egenskaber og belysningsforholdene. FAPAR er meget nyttig som input til en "
"række modeller for primær produktivitet baseret på enkle "
"effektivitetsbetragtninger."

msgid ""
"FCover is defined as the fraction of ground surface covered by green "
"vegetation as seen from the nadir direction. It is used to separate "
"vegetation and soil in energy balance processes, including temperature and "
"evapotranspiration. It is computed from the leaf area index and other "
"canopy structural variables and does not depend on variables such as the "
"geometry of illumination as compared to FAPAR. For this reason, it is a "
"very good candidate for the replacement of classical vegetation indices for "
"the monitoring of green vegetation. Because of the linear relationship with "
"radiometric signal, FCover will be only marginally scale dependent. Note "
"that similarly to LAI and FAPAR, only the green elements will be "
"considered, either belonging both to the overstory and understory."
msgstr ""
"FCover er defineret som den andel af jordoverfladen, der er dækket af grøn "
"vegetation set fra nadirretningen. Den bruges til at adskille vegetation og "
"jord i energibalanceprocesser, herunder temperatur og evapotranspiration. "
"Den beregnes ud fra bladarealindekset og andre strukturelle variable for "
"kronedækket og afhænger ikke af variable som belysningsgeometri i "
"modsætning til FAPAR. Af denne grund er den en meget god kandidat til at "
"erstatte klassiske vegetationsindeks til overvågning af grøn vegetation. På "
"grund af den lineære sammenhæng med det radiometriske signal vil FCover kun "
"være marginalt skalaafhængig. Bemærk, at der på samme måde som for LAI og "
"FAPAR kun tages hensyn til de grønne elementer, uanset om de tilhører "
"overetagen eller underetagen."

msgid ""
"Gross Primary Production (GPP) expresses a component of Primary Production "
"of ecosystems related to the creation of new organic matter by vegetation. "
"GPP is the total amount of dry matter (carbon) \"fixed\" by land plants per "
"unit time through photosynthesis (atmospheric CO2 into organic compounds). "
"A substantial fraction of GPP supports plant autotrophic respiration (Ra). "
"GPP is typically expressed as gram of carbon per square meter per day "
"(gC/m2 /day)."
msgstr ""
"Gross Primary Production (GPP) udtrykker en komponent af økosystemers "
"primærproduktion, der er knyttet til vegetationens dannelse af nyt organisk "
"stof. GPP er den samlede mængde tørstof (kulstof), der \"fikseres\" af "
"landplanter pr. tidsenhed gennem fotosyntese (atmosfærisk CO2 til organiske "
"forbindelser). En væsentlig andel af GPP understøtter planternes autotrofe "
"respiration (Ra). GPP udtrykkes typisk som gram kulstof pr. kvadratmeter "
"pr. dag (gC/m2/dag)."

msgid ""
"LAI is defined as half the developed area of photosynthetically active "
"elements of the vegetation per unit horizontal ground area. It determines "
"the size of the interface for exchange of energy (including radiation) and "
"mass between the canopy and the atmosphere. This is an intrinsic canopy "
"primary variable that should not depend on observation conditions. LAI is "
"strongly non-linearly related to reflectance. Therefore, its estimation "
"from remote sensing observations is scale dependent."
msgstr ""
"LAI er defineret som halvdelen af det udfoldede areal af vegetationens "
"fotosyntetisk aktive elementer pr. enhed vandret jordareal. Det bestemmer "
"størrelsen af grænsefladen for udveksling af energi (herunder stråling) og "
"masse mellem kronedækket og atmosfæren. Dette er en iboende primær variabel "
"for kronedækket, som ikke bør afhænge af observationsforholdene. LAI er "
"stærkt ikke-lineært relateret til reflektans. Derfor er dens estimering ud "
"fra fjernmålingsobservationer skalaafhængig."

msgid ""
"LAI is defined as half the developed area of photosynthetically active "
"elements of the vegetation per unit horizontal ground area. It determines "
